window.BP_DATA={"version":"V7 · Economics prompt V3","date":"2026-11-09","projects":[{"id":"persona","number":"01","name":"Personal AI for everyday life","position":"An accessible personal AI assistant, built around useful everyday tasks","pages":[{"number":1,"title":"Executive summary & ambition","lead":"Target 100,000 genuine paying users in 90 days, stretch to 200,000, then pursue one million and ten million.","body":"### Commercial objective\nAn accessible CNY 1 entry offer for a useful personal AI. 100,000 unique payers × 1 produces 100,000 revenue. The full economic budget is capped at 50,000, targeting 50,000 surplus. At 200,000 payers, revenue is 200,000, budget 74,000 and target surplus 126,000. These are operating goals, not measured sales.\n\nThe entry offer supplies a current-version basic assistant license, local task/note functions and 20 capped cloud-text tasks. Ongoing voice, search, long documents and external tools are priced separately. CNY 1 does not include unlimited computation. If useful experience requires higher cloud costs, revise price or funding. A later 9.9/month upgrade may be tested but contributes no assumed revenue here.\n\n**The 50,000 surplus requires team acceptance of a capped referral experiment, total service cost ≤0.10 per payer, all marketing ≤0.10 per payer, and build/operations ≤26,000.** Returning CNY 1 for every new payer cannot produce this result.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Commercial objective</h3>\n<p>An accessible CNY 1 entry offer for a useful personal AI. 100,000 unique payers × 1 produces 100,000 revenue. The full economic budget is capped at 50,000, targeting 50,000 surplus. At 200,000 payers, revenue is 200,000, budget 74,000 and target surplus 126,000. These are operating goals, not measured sales.</p>\n<p>The entry offer supplies a current-version basic assistant license, local task/note functions and 20 capped cloud-text tasks. Ongoing voice, search, long documents and external tools are priced separately. CNY 1 does not include unlimited computation. If useful experience requires higher cloud costs, revise price or funding. A later 9.9/month upgrade may be tested but contributes no assumed revenue here.</p>\n<p><strong>The 50,000 surplus requires team acceptance of a capped referral experiment, total service cost ≤0.10 per payer, all marketing ≤0.10 per payer, and build/operations ≤26,000.</strong> Returning CNY 1 for every new payer cannot produce this result.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":2,"title":"Customers & the problem","lead":"A broad ambition still needs specific launch use cases that give people a reason to return.","body":"| Initial audience hypothesis | Actual tasks | Value to test |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Students and early-career users | Read material, explain questions, organize plans | Less switching between tools; easier understanding |\n| Employees and independent workers | Draft copy, prepare meeting material, manage tasks and find information | Outputs that can be used and developed further |\n| Everyday users | Itineraries, lists, questions and personal notes | Voice input, continuity of preferences and records |\n\n### Who pays\nThe user pays a monthly fee for a real AI service. An invited person must receive independent product value; payment should not primarily buy eligibility to recruit others for rewards.\n\n### Differentiation questions\nGeneral-purpose assistants already exist. We need to test whether daily use is simpler, tasks actually get completed, personal settings carry forward, the low price includes enough usable capacity, and people share because the product helps them.\n\n### Initial cohorts\nAll three groups belong to the long-term market. The first 1,000 should be segmented rather than blended into one metric: record tasks, D7 usage, payment and referral quality by group, then decide which use cases deserve focus.","sources":["S15","S16"],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Initial audience hypothesis</th><th scope=\"col\">Actual tasks</th><th scope=\"col\">Value to test</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Students and early-career users</td><td>Read material, explain questions, organize plans</td><td>Less switching between tools; easier understanding</td></tr><tr><td>Employees and independent workers</td><td>Draft copy, prepare meeting material, manage tasks and find information</td><td>Outputs that can be used and developed further</td></tr><tr><td>Everyday users</td><td>Itineraries, lists, questions and personal notes</td><td>Voice input, continuity of preferences and records</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Who pays</h3>\n<p>The user pays a monthly fee for a real AI service. An invited person must receive independent product value; payment should not primarily buy eligibility to recruit others for rewards.</p>\n<h3>Differentiation questions</h3>\n<p>General-purpose assistants already exist. We need to test whether daily use is simpler, tasks actually get completed, personal settings carry forward, the low price includes enough usable capacity, and people share because the product helps them.</p>\n<h3>Initial cohorts</h3>\n<p>All three groups belong to the long-term market. The first 1,000 should be segmented rather than blended into one metric: record tasks, D7 usage, payment and referral quality by group, then decide which use cases deserve focus.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":3,"title":"Product & user journey","lead":"The product should connect understanding a request, processing information, producing an output, obtaining confirmation and following through.","body":"| Capability | Intended experience | Engineering questions |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Conversation and voice | Describe a question or task directly | Model quality, voice cost and latency |\n| Documents and search | Read files, extract information and retain sources | File limits, retrieval provenance and failures |\n| Useful outputs | Lists, drafts, plans and summaries | Quality, editing and export |\n| Tasks and memory | Retain approved preferences and task status | Permissions, accuracy, deletion and synchronization |\n| Optional identity | Configurable character, voice, name and tone | Asset rights and consistent behavior |\n\n### Example\n“Read this event brief, list what I need to prepare this week, draft an announcement, and remind me on Friday to confirm.” The assistant explains its understanding, organizes the material, and produces a checklist and draft. The user confirms saving and reminders. External messages, payments and other consequential actions require confirmation of the specific action and permissions.\n\n### Experience standard\nDisplay an action as completed only after it succeeds. Tool failures should show a reason and next step. A personalized identity can make the product approachable, but cannot replace task quality. Reminders and alarms are part of the capability set, not the whole product.","sources":[],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Capability</th><th scope=\"col\">Intended experience</th><th scope=\"col\">Engineering questions</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Conversation and voice</td><td>Describe a question or task directly</td><td>Model quality, voice cost and latency</td></tr><tr><td>Documents and search</td><td>Read files, extract information and retain sources</td><td>File limits, retrieval provenance and failures</td></tr><tr><td>Useful outputs</td><td>Lists, drafts, plans and summaries</td><td>Quality, editing and export</td></tr><tr><td>Tasks and memory</td><td>Retain approved preferences and task status</td><td>Permissions, accuracy, deletion and synchronization</td></tr><tr><td>Optional identity</td><td>Configurable character, voice, name and tone</td><td>Asset rights and consistent behavior</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p>“Read this event brief, list what I need to prepare this week, draft an announcement, and remind me on Friday to confirm.” The assistant explains its understanding, organizes the material, and produces a checklist and draft. The user confirms saving and reminders. External messages, payments and other consequential actions require confirmation of the specific action and permissions.</p>\n<h3>Experience standard</h3>\n<p>Display an action as completed only after it succeeds. Tool failures should show a reason and next step. A personalized identity can make the product approachable, but cannot replace task quality. Reminders and alarms are part of the capability set, not the whole product.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":4,"title":"MVP & delivery scope","lead":"The CNY 1 offer must deliver useful basic assistance with explicit, funded cloud allowances.","body":"### Launch specification — subject to joint quotation and engineering review\nCurrent-version basic license; local lists, plans and records; 20 short cloud-text tasks; task status, failures, deletion and export. Confirm fulfillment and revenue allocation between the delivered license and attached cloud service before collecting payment. Reserve the full service allowance even for late entrants or unused credits.\n\nService ceiling per payer: CNY 0.10 = model calls 0.06 + storage/network 0.02 + retries/support 0.02. Across 20 tasks, average total cost must be ≤0.005/task. Measure context/output limits, routing and caching. If supplier cost or quality cannot support this, revise the task design, price or funding before selling. Allowances and top-ups must be understandable to ordinary users.\n\nBuild ceiling: 100 engineering hours × 120 + 75 product hours × 80 = 18,000. Ninety-day operations: 100 hours × 80 = 8,000. This depends on reuse of prototypes/components; disclose and re-estimate extra work rather than excluding it.","sources":["S13","S16"],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Launch specification — subject to joint quotation and engineering review</h3>\n<p>Current-version basic license; local lists, plans and records; 20 short cloud-text tasks; task status, failures, deletion and export. Confirm fulfillment and revenue allocation between the delivered license and attached cloud service before collecting payment. Reserve the full service allowance even for late entrants or unused credits.</p>\n<p>Service ceiling per payer: CNY 0.10 = model calls 0.06 + storage/network 0.02 + retries/support 0.02. Across 20 tasks, average total cost must be ≤0.005/task. Measure context/output limits, routing and caching. If supplier cost or quality cannot support this, revise the task design, price or funding before selling. Allowances and top-ups must be understandable to ordinary users.</p>\n<p>Build ceiling: 100 engineering hours × 120 + 75 product hours × 80 = 18,000. Ninety-day operations: 100 hours × 80 = 8,000. This depends on reuse of prototypes/components; disclose and re-estimate extra work rather than excluding it.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":5,"title":"Market sizing & evidence","lead":"100,000 / 200,000 mean unique paying users. One million and ten million are later strategic stages.","body":"| Stage | User and revenue definition | Evidence required |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 90-day target: 100,000 | Real payers; CNY 100,000 revenue | Distribution, low-cost fulfillment and controlled rewards |\n| 90-day stretch: 200,000 | Real payers; CNY 200,000 revenue | Scalable channels and stable capacity |\n| One-million stage | One million payers; CNY one million entry sales | Re-estimate platform, staffing, settlement and acquisition |\n| Ten-million stage | Ten million payers; CNY ten million entry sales | Broad distribution, lasting value and professional operations |\n\nNo date is promised for later stages. Their cost figures are standalone capacity illustrations, not quotations. Macro AI adoption does not supply this project's customers. At 40% activated-to-paid conversion, 100,000 payers require 250,000 activations; at 50% visit-to-activation, that requires 500,000 unique visits.","sources":["S1"],"requirements":["R1"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Stage</th><th scope=\"col\">User and revenue definition</th><th scope=\"col\">Evidence required</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>90-day target: 100,000</td><td>Real payers; CNY 100,000 revenue</td><td>Distribution, low-cost fulfillment and controlled rewards</td></tr><tr><td>90-day stretch: 200,000</td><td>Real payers; CNY 200,000 revenue</td><td>Scalable channels and stable capacity</td></tr><tr><td>One-million stage</td><td>One million payers; CNY one million entry sales</td><td>Re-estimate platform, staffing, settlement and acquisition</td></tr><tr><td>Ten-million stage</td><td>Ten million payers; CNY ten million entry sales</td><td>Broad distribution, lasting value and professional operations</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>No date is promised for later stages. Their cost figures are standalone capacity illustrations, not quotations. Macro AI adoption does not supply this project&#x27;s customers. At 40% activated-to-paid conversion, 100,000 payers require 250,000 activations; at 50% visit-to-activation, that requires 500,000 unique visits.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":6,"title":"Competition & alternatives","lead":"Strong general-purpose alternatives already exist. Low prices and referrals must be supported by sustained usefulness.","body":"| Alternative | Existing capability / reference | Question for this product |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Doubao and other general AI assistants | Official introduction includes assistant, voice and text capabilities | Why switch? Is this simpler or better for daily tasks? |\n| Apple Intelligence | Developer material covers personal context and app actions | What additional value exists across devices, audiences or experience? |\n| A user's existing tool set | Search, documents, calendar, notes and AI chat | Does the product reduce steps and complete more tasks? |\n| Character.AI / Replika | Established character or companion experiences | How does personalization strengthen usefulness beyond appearance? |\n\n### First comparison\nUse 10–20 frequent tasks. Ask users to try both their current tools and the prototype. Measure completion, elapsed time, edits, instructions required, cost and a second self-initiated use.\n\n### Advantages to prove\nDo not claim stronger models than major platforms, universally lower costs or an existing data moat without evidence. Test simpler access, executable tasks, continuous personal settings and accessible pricing. Referral incentives are an acquisition mechanism, not a durable product advantage by themselves.","sources":["S15","S16","S3","S5"],"requirements":["R1","R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Alternative</th><th scope=\"col\">Existing capability / reference</th><th scope=\"col\">Question for this product</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Doubao and other general AI assistants</td><td>Official introduction includes assistant, voice and text capabilities</td><td>Why switch? Is this simpler or better for daily tasks?</td></tr><tr><td>Apple Intelligence</td><td>Developer material covers personal context and app actions</td><td>What additional value exists across devices, audiences or experience?</td></tr><tr><td>A user&#x27;s existing tool set</td><td>Search, documents, calendar, notes and AI chat</td><td>Does the product reduce steps and complete more tasks?</td></tr><tr><td>Character.AI / Replika</td><td>Established character or companion experiences</td><td>How does personalization strengthen usefulness beyond appearance?</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>First comparison</h3>\n<p>Use 10–20 frequent tasks. Ask users to try both their current tools and the prototype. Measure completion, elapsed time, edits, instructions required, cost and a second self-initiated use.</p>\n<h3>Advantages to prove</h3>\n<p>Do not claim stronger models than major platforms, universally lower costs or an existing data moat without evidence. Test simpler access, executable tasks, continuous personal settings and accessible pricing. Referral incentives are an acquisition mechanism, not a durable product advantage by themselves.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":7,"title":"Business model & pricing","lead":"Count actual CNY 1 entry sales; later subscriptions do not fill the target profit gap.","body":"### Price and entitlement\nCNY 1 once for the current basic version and capped cloud allowances, without unlimited voice or indefinite unlimited service. Test an enhanced 9.9/month tier separately with its own scope, renewal and costs; its revenue is excluded. A 1/month alternative remains discussable, but must use actual paying customer-months rather than assuming everyone pays for three months.\n\n### Referral decision to make together\nThe target case funds the first 5,000 eligible direct referred first payments at CNY 1 each: a 5,000 total pool. Stop at the cap or approve a new batch; promise no cash outside the pool. Disclose eligibility, remaining capacity, refund observation and settlement before the campaign. Multiple valid direct referrals can earn rewards without multiple commission levels.\n\nThis changes the original all-payments-returned concept and needs team agreement. Keeping a full CNY 1 reward on every CNY 1 purchase requires another identified revenue source. It cannot simultaneously deliver 100,000 revenue, 50,000 total costs and 50,000 profit.","sources":["S13","S14"],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Price and entitlement</h3>\n<p>CNY 1 once for the current basic version and capped cloud allowances, without unlimited voice or indefinite unlimited service. Test an enhanced 9.9/month tier separately with its own scope, renewal and costs; its revenue is excluded. A 1/month alternative remains discussable, but must use actual paying customer-months rather than assuming everyone pays for three months.</p>\n<h3>Referral decision to make together</h3>\n<p>The target case funds the first 5,000 eligible direct referred first payments at CNY 1 each: a 5,000 total pool. Stop at the cap or approve a new batch; promise no cash outside the pool. Disclose eligibility, remaining capacity, refund observation and settlement before the campaign. Multiple valid direct referrals can earn rewards without multiple commission levels.</p>\n<p>This changes the original all-payments-returned concept and needs team agreement. Keeping a full CNY 1 reward on every CNY 1 purchase requires another identified revenue source. It cannot simultaneously deliver 100,000 revenue, 50,000 total costs and 50,000 profit.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":8,"title":"Unit economics & viability","lead":"At 100,000 payers, target cost is CNY 0.50 each: 0.24 variable and 0.26 allocated fixed cost.","body":"| Cost item | CNY budget |\n| --- | --- |\n| Build and operating labor | 26,000.00 |\n| Models and infrastructure allowances | 10,000.00 |\n| Processing and tax/refund reserve | 4,000.00 |\n| Seed/content marketing | 5,000.00 |\n| Capped referral reward pool | 5,000.00 |\n\n100,000 revenue − 10,000 service − 4,000 processing/tax/refund reserve − 5,000 seed marketing − 5,000 rewards − 26,000 build/operations = 50,000 target surplus. Processing assumes 1%, combined tax/refund reserve 3%; neither is a quote or tax opinion. If a selected store charges commission, replace the channel assumption.\n\nBreak-even = 26,000 / 0.76, rounded up to 34,211 payers. At 0.40 service cost per payer, target surplus falls to 20,000. With a CNY 1 reward for every payer, rewards rise from 5,000 to 100,000 and surplus becomes −45,000. An additional applicable 30% store fee would reduce surplus to 20,000 if all else stayed constant.\n\nTwenty tasks each imply two million tasks. The 0.06/payer model ceiling means 6,000 total model budget. Suppliers bill input/output separately: measure tokens, retries, cache hits and logs. Do not claim this cost has been achieved before load and quality testing.\n\nTencent TokenHub S17 (checked 2026-11-09) lists Hy3 at CNY 1/million input tokens and 4/million output tokens. Budget illustration only: 1,000 input + 500 output tokens costs 0.003/task, or 0.06 for 20 tasks. Actual context, quality, retries and model selection still require validation.","sources":["S17"],"requirements":["R1","R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cost item</th><th scope=\"col\">CNY budget</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Build and operating labor</td><td>26,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Models and infrastructure allowances</td><td>10,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Processing and tax/refund reserve</td><td>4,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Seed/content marketing</td><td>5,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Capped referral reward pool</td><td>5,000.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>100,000 revenue − 10,000 service − 4,000 processing/tax/refund reserve − 5,000 seed marketing − 5,000 rewards − 26,000 build/operations = 50,000 target surplus. Processing assumes 1%, combined tax/refund reserve 3%; neither is a quote or tax opinion. If a selected store charges commission, replace the channel assumption.</p>\n<p>Break-even = 26,000 / 0.76, rounded up to 34,211 payers. At 0.40 service cost per payer, target surplus falls to 20,000. With a CNY 1 reward for every payer, rewards rise from 5,000 to 100,000 and surplus becomes −45,000. An additional applicable 30% store fee would reduce surplus to 20,000 if all else stayed constant.</p>\n<p>Twenty tasks each imply two million tasks. The 0.06/payer model ceiling means 6,000 total model budget. Suppliers bill input/output separately: measure tokens, retries, cache hits and logs. Do not claim this cost has been achieved before load and quality testing.</p>\n<p>Tencent TokenHub S17 (checked 2026-11-09) lists Hy3 at CNY 1/million input tokens and 4/million output tokens. Budget illustration only: 1,000 input + 500 output tokens costs 0.003/task, or 0.06 for 20 tasks. Actual context, quality, retries and model selection still require validation.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":9,"title":"First 100,000 paying users","lead":"The 90-day target needs 500,000 unique visits; a small seed group alone does not establish this reach.","body":"| Channel assumption | Unique visits | Execution |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 50 creator/community entries | 50 × 6,000 = 300,000 | 200 prospects → 100 substantive discussions → 50 agreements, each with demonstration and attribution |\n| Owned/joint task demonstrations | 100,000 | 100 task demonstrations averaging 1,000 actual visits, not video views |\n| User sharing and search discovery | 100,000 | Share useful outputs; remove overlap, self-referrals and invalid payments |\n| Total | 500,000 | 50% activation × 40% payment = 100,000 |\n\nNo partnerships or traffic are confirmed. CNY 0.10 all-in marketing per payer requires substantial organic/owned distribution, not an assumption that 10,000 buys 100,000 customers. The 5,000 seed/content budget covers assets/tools, not unquoted creator placement fees. Recalculate for paid partners. Within 14 days, obtain at least ten actual channel agreements and attributable visit/payment evidence; otherwise disclose the reach gap and revise channels, timing or funding.","sources":[],"requirements":["R3"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Channel assumption</th><th scope=\"col\">Unique visits</th><th scope=\"col\">Execution</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>50 creator/community entries</td><td>50 × 6,000 = 300,000</td><td>200 prospects → 100 substantive discussions → 50 agreements, each with demonstration and attribution</td></tr><tr><td>Owned/joint task demonstrations</td><td>100,000</td><td>100 task demonstrations averaging 1,000 actual visits, not video views</td></tr><tr><td>User sharing and search discovery</td><td>100,000</td><td>Share useful outputs; remove overlap, self-referrals and invalid payments</td></tr><tr><td>Total</td><td>500,000</td><td>50% activation × 40% payment = 100,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>No partnerships or traffic are confirmed. CNY 0.10 all-in marketing per payer requires substantial organic/owned distribution, not an assumption that 10,000 buys 100,000 customers. The 5,000 seed/content budget covers assets/tools, not unquoted creator placement fees. Recalculate for paid partners. Within 14 days, obtain at least ten actual channel agreements and attributable visit/payment evidence; otherwise disclose the reach gap and revise channels, timing or funding.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":10,"title":"CNY 1 referrals & the growth model","lead":"Referrals are a capped growth experiment. The 100,000 goal needs both channel reach and measured sharing.","body":"### Two mechanisms, different results\nAt 100,000 payers × CNY 1, rewarding every payer costs 100,000. Other costs of 45,000 produce a −45,000 result. Capping rewards at 5,000 produces a 50,000 total budget and 50,000 target surplus. Future financing does not turn a current loss into profit.\n\n### Propagation and timing\nK = sharing participation × unique invitations × activation × payment. For example, 50% × 5 × 50% × 40% = 0.50; 80% × 8 × 50% × 40% = 1.28. Measure the latter; K may fall when incentives end. Separate incentivized and organic cohorts. The 500,000-visit funnel already includes sharing traffic: do not add the same referred users twice.\n\nAttribution → activation → genuine payment → refund observation → verification → record within the pool → settlement. Disclose pool balance/end conditions and review applicable channel rules. If the team retains full CNY 1 rewards for everyone, discuss a genuinely valuable CNY 10 product, sponsorship or other signed revenue; include none before it exists.","sources":[],"requirements":["R3"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Two mechanisms, different results</h3>\n<p>At 100,000 payers × CNY 1, rewarding every payer costs 100,000. Other costs of 45,000 produce a −45,000 result. Capping rewards at 5,000 produces a 50,000 total budget and 50,000 target surplus. Future financing does not turn a current loss into profit.</p>\n<h3>Propagation and timing</h3>\n<p>K = sharing participation × unique invitations × activation × payment. For example, 50% × 5 × 50% × 40% = 0.50; 80% × 8 × 50% × 40% = 1.28. Measure the latter; K may fall when incentives end. Separate incentivized and organic cohorts. The 500,000-visit funnel already includes sharing traffic: do not add the same referred users twice.</p>\n<p>Attribution → activation → genuine payment → refund observation → verification → record within the pool → settlement. Disclose pool balance/end conditions and review applicable channel rules. If the team retains full CNY 1 rewards for everyone, discuss a genuinely valuable CNY 10 product, sponsorship or other signed revenue; include none before it exists.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":11,"title":"90-day economics & scale targets","lead":"100,000 is the 90-day operating target; 200,000 is stretch. Later scale rows are standalone illustrations.","body":"| Scenario / stage | Paying customers | Revenue | Total budget | Target economic surplus |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Conservative | 30,000 | 30,000.00 | 33,200.00 | -3,200.00 |\n| Target | 100,000 | 100,000.00 | 50,000.00 | 50,000.00 |\n| Stretch | 200,000 | 200,000.00 | 74,000.00 | 126,000.00 |\n| One-million stage | 1,000,000 | 1,000,000.00 | 360,000.00 | 640,000.00 |\n| Ten-million stage | 10,000,000 | 10,000,000.00 | 3,400,000.00 | 6,600,000.00 |\n\n### Basis of calculation\nThis is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit.\nLater fixed build/operations placeholders are 120,000 at one million and one million at ten million, subject to fresh quotations. These are not 90-day promises or repeat revenue from the same users. The conservative case loses money, showing why reach and cost evidence are required.","sources":[],"requirements":["R1","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Scenario / stage</th><th scope=\"col\">Paying customers</th><th scope=\"col\">Revenue</th><th scope=\"col\">Total budget</th><th scope=\"col\">Target economic surplus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Conservative</td><td>30,000</td><td>30,000.00</td><td>33,200.00</td><td>-3,200.00</td></tr><tr><td>Target</td><td>100,000</td><td>100,000.00</td><td>50,000.00</td><td>50,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Stretch</td><td>200,000</td><td>200,000.00</td><td>74,000.00</td><td>126,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>One-million stage</td><td>1,000,000</td><td>1,000,000.00</td><td>360,000.00</td><td>640,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Ten-million stage</td><td>10,000,000</td><td>10,000,000.00</td><td>3,400,000.00</td><td>6,600,000.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Basis of calculation</h3>\n<p>This is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit. Later fixed build/operations placeholders are 120,000 at one million and one million at ten million, subject to fresh quotations. These are not 90-day promises or repeat revenue from the same users. The conservative case loses money, showing why reach and cost evidence are required.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":12,"title":"Resources & cash planning","lead":"The target CNY 50,000 is the full economic budget, not server costs alone.","body":"| Cost item | CNY budget |\n| --- | --- |\n| Build and operating labor | 26,000.00 |\n| Models and infrastructure allowances | 10,000.00 |\n| Processing and tax/refund reserve | 4,000.00 |\n| Seed/content marketing | 5,000.00 |\n| Capped referral reward pool | 5,000.00 |\n\n### Funding\nPrefer to secure the full 50,000 budget rather than depend on immediate payment withdrawals. Retain refund reserves and unconsumed cloud-service liabilities. Illustrative monthly spending: 24,000 / 12,000 / 14,000. If 20,000 / 30,000 / 50,000 payments are settled, cumulative month-end balances are −4,000 / 14,000 / 50,000. This simplified month-end view excludes daily peaks and settlement holds; prepare a dated cash ledger.\n\n### Approval gates\nRelease 10,000 for the first 14 days to validate quality, cost and reach. The 50,000 target budget is an expansion cap, not automatic spending authority. The 18,000 build is already included. Native dual-platform development, paid review or store commissions require a revised budget.","sources":[],"requirements":["R1"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cost item</th><th scope=\"col\">CNY budget</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Build and operating labor</td><td>26,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Models and infrastructure allowances</td><td>10,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Processing and tax/refund reserve</td><td>4,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Seed/content marketing</td><td>5,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Capped referral reward pool</td><td>5,000.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Funding</h3>\n<p>Prefer to secure the full 50,000 budget rather than depend on immediate payment withdrawals. Retain refund reserves and unconsumed cloud-service liabilities. Illustrative monthly spending: 24,000 / 12,000 / 14,000. If 20,000 / 30,000 / 50,000 payments are settled, cumulative month-end balances are −4,000 / 14,000 / 50,000. This simplified month-end view excludes daily peaks and settlement holds; prepare a dated cash ledger.</p>\n<h3>Approval gates</h3>\n<p>Release 10,000 for the first 14 days to validate quality, cost and reach. The 50,000 target budget is an expansion cap, not automatic spending authority. The 18,000 build is already included. Native dual-platform development, paid review or store commissions require a revised budget.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":13,"title":"90-day milestones","lead":"Plan 20,000 / 30,000 / 50,000 new payers by month, revising when evidence falls short.","body":"| Checkpoint | Target and action | Decision |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| D7 | Core tasks, payment and cost logs; 100 real-task users | Validate delivered value and task cost |\n| D14 | Ten agreed distribution entries; 1,000-payer validation batch | Check payments, refunds, cost and non-incentivized use |\n| D30 | 20,000 total payers in month one; build toward 50 entries | Recalculate from the real funnel if behind |\n| D60 | 30,000 additional, 50,000 cumulative | Stop expansion if quality, channels or costs fail |\n| D90 | 50,000 additional, 100,000 cumulative; 200,000 stretch | Reconcile fulfillment, reserves, surplus and next stage |\n\nChannels have not established this pace. Schedule one-million and ten-million stages jointly after actual 100,000 payments, 30-day task retention and cost/quality evidence; a low price alone does not establish fast growth.","sources":[],"requirements":["R3","R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Checkpoint</th><th scope=\"col\">Target and action</th><th scope=\"col\">Decision</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>D7</td><td>Core tasks, payment and cost logs; 100 real-task users</td><td>Validate delivered value and task cost</td></tr><tr><td>D14</td><td>Ten agreed distribution entries; 1,000-payer validation batch</td><td>Check payments, refunds, cost and non-incentivized use</td></tr><tr><td>D30</td><td>20,000 total payers in month one; build toward 50 entries</td><td>Recalculate from the real funnel if behind</td></tr><tr><td>D60</td><td>30,000 additional, 50,000 cumulative</td><td>Stop expansion if quality, channels or costs fail</td></tr><tr><td>D90</td><td>50,000 additional, 100,000 cumulative; 200,000 stretch</td><td>Reconcile fulfillment, reserves, surplus and next stage</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Channels have not established this pace. Schedule one-million and ten-million stages jointly after actual 100,000 payments, 30-day task retention and cost/quality evidence; a low price alone does not establish fast growth.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":14,"title":"Metrics & acceptance criteria","lead":"Assess payment, fulfillment, cost and quality together rather than revenue alone.","body":"100,000 genuine payers; 500,000 visits; service ≤0.10/payer; all marketing ≤0.10/payer; 30-day task activity ≥25%; budget ≤50,000.\n\nThese are proposed thresholds. Count unique valid payers, remove invalid/refunded transactions, and accept only usable confirmed outputs. Separate mature observation periods. Track source, reach, unique visits, actual payment, delivery, refunds and full cost. Downloads and intent are not revenue. Pause expansion and revise the plan if early pricing, quality or unit-cost gates fail.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>100,000 genuine payers; 500,000 visits; service ≤0.10/payer; all marketing ≤0.10/payer; 30-day task activity ≥25%; budget ≤50,000.</p>\n<p>These are proposed thresholds. Count unique valid payers, remove invalid/refunded transactions, and accept only usable confirmed outputs. Separate mature observation periods. Track source, reach, unique visits, actual payment, delivery, refunds and full cost. Downloads and intent are not revenue. Pause expansion and revise the plan if early pricing, quality or unit-cost gates fail.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":15,"title":"Risks & responses","lead":"Use transparent rules to manage promotion and service costs; a small transaction can create a large cumulative obligation.","body":"| Risk | Condition to check | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Rewards consume revenue | Service costs remain after returning the first CNY 1 | Budget subsidy, test renewal contribution or change rewards |\n| Fake payments / self-referrals | Account, device, payment and refund anomalies | Reward only genuine eligible new customers; observation period and appeal |\n| Platform and launch rules | Specific platform, region, payment route and reward mechanics | Check applicable rules and professional advice before finalizing launch |\n| Payment buys recruitment eligibility | Purchasing is framed as joining a referral-income network | Ensure genuine service value; no paid recruiting qualification or tiered commissions |\n| Cost and capacity | Heavy usage, tool failures and traffic spikes | Allowances, monitoring, load tests and transparent failures |\n| Personal data and execution | Memory, documents and external-action permissions | Least privilege, explicit confirmation, deletion and access logs |\n\n### Scope of rules review\nApple has rules concerning paid functionality and incentives. Application depends on region and mechanics; do not assume paid installation plus cash referrals can launch unchanged. China's Regulations on Prohibition of Pyramid Selling address, among other situations, payment for recruiting eligibility and compensation based on recruitment or levels. A single level does not automatically establish compliance; the actual structure requires professional assessment.\n\nThis review informs a workable version of the growth concept. It does not replace the business discussion. No cashback program is open and no money has been collected through this BP.","sources":["S13","S14"],"requirements":["R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Risk</th><th scope=\"col\">Condition to check</th><th scope=\"col\">Response</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rewards consume revenue</td><td>Service costs remain after returning the first CNY 1</td><td>Budget subsidy, test renewal contribution or change rewards</td></tr><tr><td>Fake payments / self-referrals</td><td>Account, device, payment and refund anomalies</td><td>Reward only genuine eligible new customers; observation period and appeal</td></tr><tr><td>Platform and launch rules</td><td>Specific platform, region, payment route and reward mechanics</td><td>Check applicable rules and professional advice before finalizing launch</td></tr><tr><td>Payment buys recruitment eligibility</td><td>Purchasing is framed as joining a referral-income network</td><td>Ensure genuine service value; no paid recruiting qualification or tiered commissions</td></tr><tr><td>Cost and capacity</td><td>Heavy usage, tool failures and traffic spikes</td><td>Allowances, monitoring, load tests and transparent failures</td></tr><tr><td>Personal data and execution</td><td>Memory, documents and external-action permissions</td><td>Least privilege, explicit confirmation, deletion and access logs</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Scope of rules review</h3>\n<p>Apple has rules concerning paid functionality and incentives. Application depends on region and mechanics; do not assume paid installation plus cash referrals can launch unchanged. China&#x27;s Regulations on Prohibition of Pyramid Selling address, among other situations, payment for recruiting eligibility and compensation based on recruitment or levels. A single level does not automatically establish compliance; the actual structure requires professional assessment.</p>\n<p>This review informs a workable version of the growth concept. It does not replace the business discussion. No cashback program is open and no money has been collected through this BP.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":16,"title":"Team roles & collaboration","lead":"I will lead product and market execution, while assessing technical choices and resources jointly with the team.","body":"### My proposed responsibilities\nI will own everyday needs and task experience, pricing and referral experiments, channel content and user feedback. I can rapidly prototype and prepare experiments with AI, and want to assess reliability, costs and scalable implementation with engineering. A prototype is not proof of production-service readiness.\n\n| Role | Proposed responsibility | To confirm |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 最高 | Product, customers/users, market work, experiments and review | Availability and stage targets |\n| Engineering lead | Architecture, models/tools, permissions, tasks and cost logs | People, hours, schedule and maintenance |\n| Professional / content reviewer | Facts, asset rights and output quality | Reviewer, competence, price and scope |\n| Customer / user | Usable material, confirmation, feedback and acceptance | Consent and intended use |\n| Team247 lead | Budget, resources, payment/contract entity and stage decisions | Authority and available resources |\n\n### Decisions to make together\nLaunch platform, core tasks, models/tools, usage budget, data handling, release requirements, price, responsibilities and acceptance. Joint discussion is not an excuse to provide no proposal: this BP offers comparable assumptions and experiments for the team to revise.\n\n### Working cadence\nReview real activations/customers, payments/refunds, output quality, effort/API costs and next-week decisions weekly. Record a continue/adjust/pause decision at days 14 and 30. These are proposals, not staffing or budget commitments already obtained.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>My proposed responsibilities</h3>\n<p>I will own everyday needs and task experience, pricing and referral experiments, channel content and user feedback. I can rapidly prototype and prepare experiments with AI, and want to assess reliability, costs and scalable implementation with engineering. A prototype is not proof of production-service readiness.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Role</th><th scope=\"col\">Proposed responsibility</th><th scope=\"col\">To confirm</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>最高</td><td>Product, customers/users, market work, experiments and review</td><td>Availability and stage targets</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering lead</td><td>Architecture, models/tools, permissions, tasks and cost logs</td><td>People, hours, schedule and maintenance</td></tr><tr><td>Professional / content reviewer</td><td>Facts, asset rights and output quality</td><td>Reviewer, competence, price and scope</td></tr><tr><td>Customer / user</td><td>Usable material, confirmation, feedback and acceptance</td><td>Consent and intended use</td></tr><tr><td>Team247 lead</td><td>Budget, resources, payment/contract entity and stage decisions</td><td>Authority and available resources</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Decisions to make together</h3>\n<p>Launch platform, core tasks, models/tools, usage budget, data handling, release requirements, price, responsibilities and acceptance. Joint discussion is not an excuse to provide no proposal: this BP offers comparable assumptions and experiments for the team to revise.</p>\n<h3>Working cadence</h3>\n<p>Review real activations/customers, payments/refunds, output quality, effort/API costs and next-week decisions weekly. Record a continue/adjust/pause decision at days 14 and 30. These are proposals, not staffing or budget commitments already obtained.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":17,"title":"Evidence, assumptions & unknowns","lead":"Public sources support context and constraints. Project revenue and growth remain unverified assumptions.","body":"| Evidence | Date and limits |\n| --- | --- |\n| [S1 · CNNIC: 2026 generative AI application report](https://www2.cnnic.cn/n4/2026/1008/c326-11703.html) | Published 2026-10-08; first half of 2026. Official indexed summary only; direct body retrieval timed out. More than 700 million AI users is context, not the size of this paying segment. |\n| [S13 · Apple App Review Guidelines](https://developer.apple.com/app-store/review/guidelines/) | Checked 2026-11-09. Paid functionality, incentives and store rules need assessment for the relevant region and actual mechanism; cash rewards cannot be assumed launchable unchanged. |\n| [S14 · Ministry of Justice: Regulations on Prohibition of Pyramid Selling](https://xzfg.moj.gov.cn/front/law/detail?LawID=148) | Searched 2026-11-09. Recruiting eligibility purchased through payment and compensation linked to recruitment or levels require assessment. A single referral level does not automatically establish compliance. |\n| [S15 · Doubao official feature introduction](https://www.doubao.com/legal/feature_intro) | Official indexed summary checked 2026-11-09. Assistant, voice and text capabilities. No pricing or user data from imitation websites is used. |\n| [S16 · Apple Intelligence developer introduction](https://developer.apple.com/cn/apple-intelligence/) | Official indexed summary checked 2026-11-09. Personal context, app actions and system entry points are competitive references. Region/device availability requires separate verification. |\n\n### Critical gaps\nVerified audience/channel figures; real CNY 1/10 conversion; referral K and generation time; monthly retention; measured task cost; executable reward rules; technical and staffing quotations.\n\n### Replace assumptions with evidence\nUse sourced prospect records, interviews, payment/refund records, task logs, supplier invoices and mature-cohort observations. Mark missing evidence as unverified; do not invent customers, case-study revenue, permissions or testimonials.\n\n### Evidence levels\nPublic facts retain their sources and dates. Prices, counts and costs are planning assumptions. Formula outputs are calculations. Relationships, resources and technical capability remain to be validated. Recheck dynamic prices before launch. The BP and website are deliverables; commercial viability has not been established.\n\nNew target gaps: accepted quotations, attributable reach, actual payment/refunds, full labor/API costs, delivery capacity and team resources. Page 11 economics V7 supersedes earlier figures; public sources do not establish project sales.","sources":["S1","S15","S16","S13","S14"],"requirements":["R1","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Evidence</th><th scope=\"col\">Date and limits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://www2.cnnic.cn/n4/2026/1008/c326-11703.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S1 · CNNIC: 2026 generative AI application report</a></td><td>Published 2026-10-08; first half of 2026. Official indexed summary only; direct body retrieval timed out. More than 700 million AI users is context, not the size of this paying segment.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/app-store/review/guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S13 · Apple App Review Guidelines</a></td><td>Checked 2026-11-09. Paid functionality, incentives and store rules need assessment for the relevant region and actual mechanism; cash rewards cannot be assumed launchable unchanged.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://xzfg.moj.gov.cn/front/law/detail?LawID=148\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S14 · Ministry of Justice: Regulations on Prohibition of Pyramid Selling</a></td><td>Searched 2026-11-09. Recruiting eligibility purchased through payment and compensation linked to recruitment or levels require assessment. A single referral level does not automatically establish compliance.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.doubao.com/legal/feature_intro\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S15 · Doubao official feature introduction</a></td><td>Official indexed summary checked 2026-11-09. Assistant, voice and text capabilities. No pricing or user data from imitation websites is used.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/cn/apple-intelligence/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S16 · Apple Intelligence developer introduction</a></td><td>Official indexed summary checked 2026-11-09. Personal context, app actions and system entry points are competitive references. Region/device availability requires separate verification.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Critical gaps</h3>\n<p>Verified audience/channel figures; real CNY 1/10 conversion; referral K and generation time; monthly retention; measured task cost; executable reward rules; technical and staffing quotations.</p>\n<h3>Replace assumptions with evidence</h3>\n<p>Use sourced prospect records, interviews, payment/refund records, task logs, supplier invoices and mature-cohort observations. Mark missing evidence as unverified; do not invent customers, case-study revenue, permissions or testimonials.</p>\n<h3>Evidence levels</h3>\n<p>Public facts retain their sources and dates. Prices, counts and costs are planning assumptions. Formula outputs are calculations. Relationships, resources and technical capability remain to be validated. Recheck dynamic prices before launch. The BP and website are deliverables; commercial viability has not been established.</p>\n<p>New target gaps: accepted quotations, attributable reach, actual payment/refunds, full labor/API costs, delivery capacity and team resources. Page 11 economics V7 supersedes earlier figures; public sources do not establish project sales.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":18,"title":"Recommendation & decisions","lead":"Organize resources around the larger commercial objective; target economic surplus of CNY 50,000.00 requires its assumptions to hold.","body":"Target 100,000 payers in 90 days, stretch 200,000, then pursue one million and ten million. Agree the CNY 1 scope, capped rewards, distribution commitments and service cost; pursue 20,000/30,000/50,000 monthly payers.\n\nConfirm owners, available labor, technical route, budget, operating/tax entity, channels and stop gates together. I will drive product, market, content and validation. These are the business outcomes to pursue; orders, reach and costs still require evidence. Recalculate actual results when targets are missed rather than promising profit.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Target 100,000 payers in 90 days, stretch 200,000, then pursue one million and ten million. Agree the CNY 1 scope, capped rewards, distribution commitments and service cost; pursue 20,000/30,000/50,000 monthly payers.</p>\n<p>Confirm owners, available labor, technical route, budget, operating/tax entity, channels and stop gates together. I will drive product, market, content and validation. These are the business outcomes to pursue; orders, reach and costs still require evidence. Recalculate actual results when targets are missed rather than promising profit.</p>","appendixHtml":""}]},{"id":"industry","number":"02","name":"AI agent for medical aesthetics","position":"From professional source material to reviewable business outputs","pages":[{"number":1,"title":"Executive summary","lead":"Target 12 implementations and eight service customer-months in 90 days: CNY 292,000 revenue and 102,640 economic surplus.","body":"### Higher-value implementation\nCNY 19,800 per institution delivers one running source/content workflow: one brand/business line; at most 30 documents and 200 pages; versioned retrieval; ten individually reviewed outputs; three template graphics; roles/logs; training; baseline and acceptance report; and two in-scope revision rounds. Delivery is 14 days after complete inputs. Maintenance begins the next month at 6,800/month: three seats, 30 bounded drafts, ten graphics, 100 retrievals, eight operations hours and four professional sampling/issue hours. Customers retain final per-item review; quote excess work.\n\nPrice the implementation, evidence and collaboration process, not a model interface alone. Qualify only customers with measurable labor/vendor-replacement value supporting 6,800/month. At an actual customer rate of 150/hour, at least 45.34 hours/month must be saved, or other evidenced replacement value supplied. Do not invent incremental sales to justify the price.\n","sources":[],"requirements":["R4","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Higher-value implementation</h3>\n<p>CNY 19,800 per institution delivers one running source/content workflow: one brand/business line; at most 30 documents and 200 pages; versioned retrieval; ten individually reviewed outputs; three template graphics; roles/logs; training; baseline and acceptance report; and two in-scope revision rounds. Delivery is 14 days after complete inputs. Maintenance begins the next month at 6,800/month: three seats, 30 bounded drafts, ten graphics, 100 retrievals, eight operations hours and four professional sampling/issue hours. Customers retain final per-item review; quote excess work.</p>\n<p>Price the implementation, evidence and collaboration process, not a model interface alone. Qualify only customers with measurable labor/vendor-replacement value supporting 6,800/month. At an actual customer rate of 150/hour, at least 45.34 hours/month must be saved, or other evidenced replacement value supplied. Do not invent incremental sales to justify the price.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":2,"title":"Customers & the problem","lead":"The user, reviewer and budget owner are different roles. All three must be identified.","body":"| Role | Assumed current problem | Product response | Purchasing question |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Content / operations | Repeated research, revisions and version confusion | Generate sourced drafts and template graphics from controlled material | Does editing effort actually fall? |\n| Professional reviewer | Unsupported statements and confused applicability | Inspect sources, conflicts and revision history | Can conclusions be traced and unsupported claims rejected? |\n| Business owner | Unpredictable labor and supplier delivery | See time, outputs and acceptance records | Is measurable value greater than price? |\n| Brand development | Inaccurate institution lists and slow research | Review 50 public target institutions and matching reasons | Are these qualified leads, without a sales guarantee? |\n\nA qualified pilot customer has recurring content tasks; can supply usable material; appoints both a reviewer and business owner; provides a workflow baseline; and can authorize CNY 19,800. General curiosity about AI is insufficient.\n\n### Exclusions\nNo actual task, no usable source material, no reviewer, no budget authority, or a request to replace clinical decisions means no paid pilot. Start by reconstructing a recent real task, not asking whether the prospect wants AI.","sources":[],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Role</th><th scope=\"col\">Assumed current problem</th><th scope=\"col\">Product response</th><th scope=\"col\">Purchasing question</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Content / operations</td><td>Repeated research, revisions and version confusion</td><td>Generate sourced drafts and template graphics from controlled material</td><td>Does editing effort actually fall?</td></tr><tr><td>Professional reviewer</td><td>Unsupported statements and confused applicability</td><td>Inspect sources, conflicts and revision history</td><td>Can conclusions be traced and unsupported claims rejected?</td></tr><tr><td>Business owner</td><td>Unpredictable labor and supplier delivery</td><td>See time, outputs and acceptance records</td><td>Is measurable value greater than price?</td></tr><tr><td>Brand development</td><td>Inaccurate institution lists and slow research</td><td>Review 50 public target institutions and matching reasons</td><td>Are these qualified leads, without a sales guarantee?</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>A qualified pilot customer has recurring content tasks; can supply usable material; appoints both a reviewer and business owner; provides a workflow baseline; and can authorize CNY 19,800. General curiosity about AI is insufficient.</p>\n<h3>Exclusions</h3>\n<p>No actual task, no usable source material, no reviewer, no budget authority, or a request to replace clinical decisions means no paid pilot. Start by reconstructing a recent real task, not asking whether the prospect wants AI.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":3,"title":"Product & user journey","lead":"Value comes from a complete workflow for sources, versions, review and deliverables.","body":"### From source material to a usable output\nConfirm model / market version / intended use → import authorized material → record provenance and update dates → retrieve and draft with citations → professional review → template layout → customer acceptance → version archive.\n\n### Example\nA customer requests a 500-Chinese-character product brief. Confirm the exact product and version instead of inferring intended users from the brand. List source conflicts or missing evidence. The reviewer removes unsupported statements and preserves provenance before graphics are prepared. Measure generation, verification and editing together.\n\n| Capability | What the customer receives | What cannot yet be claimed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Retrieval | Sourced facts and explicit gaps | A comprehensive proprietary industry moat |\n| Drafting | Reviewable copy or scripts | Automatically lawful publication |\n| Institution research | Deduplicated organizations, public business entry points and matching reasons | An email address equals a qualified opportunity |\n| Custom workflow | Tools and acceptance within a defined scope | Universal applicability or unlimited customization |\n\nPublic institution research is a separate add-on experiment. The customer reviews and contacts prospects through permitted channels; messages sent are not sales.","sources":["S10","S11"],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>From source material to a usable output</h3>\n<p>Confirm model / market version / intended use → import authorized material → record provenance and update dates → retrieve and draft with citations → professional review → template layout → customer acceptance → version archive.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p>A customer requests a 500-Chinese-character product brief. Confirm the exact product and version instead of inferring intended users from the brand. List source conflicts or missing evidence. The reviewer removes unsupported statements and preserves provenance before graphics are prepared. Measure generation, verification and editing together.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Capability</th><th scope=\"col\">What the customer receives</th><th scope=\"col\">What cannot yet be claimed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Retrieval</td><td>Sourced facts and explicit gaps</td><td>A comprehensive proprietary industry moat</td></tr><tr><td>Drafting</td><td>Reviewable copy or scripts</td><td>Automatically lawful publication</td></tr><tr><td>Institution research</td><td>Deduplicated organizations, public business entry points and matching reasons</td><td>An email address equals a qualified opportunity</td></tr><tr><td>Custom workflow</td><td>Tools and acceptance within a defined scope</td><td>Universal applicability or unlimited customization</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Public institution research is a separate add-on experiment. The customer reviews and contacts prospects through permitted channels; messages sent are not sales.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":4,"title":"MVP & delivery scope","lead":"Higher pricing buys a complete implementation and bounded maintenance, not regulatory approval.","body":"### Higher-value implementation\nCNY 19,800 per institution delivers one running source/content workflow: one brand/business line; at most 30 documents and 200 pages; versioned retrieval; ten individually reviewed outputs; three template graphics; roles/logs; training; baseline and acceptance report; and two in-scope revision rounds. Delivery is 14 days after complete inputs. Maintenance begins the next month at 6,800/month: three seats, 30 bounded drafts, ten graphics, 100 retrievals, eight operations hours and four professional sampling/issue hours. Customers retain final per-item review; quote excess work.\n\nPrice the implementation, evidence and collaboration process, not a model interface alone. Qualify only customers with measurable labor/vendor-replacement value supporting 6,800/month. At an actual customer rate of 150/hour, at least 45.34 hours/month must be saved, or other evidenced replacement value supplied. Do not invent incremental sales to justify the price.\n","sources":["S10","S11"],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Higher-value implementation</h3>\n<p>CNY 19,800 per institution delivers one running source/content workflow: one brand/business line; at most 30 documents and 200 pages; versioned retrieval; ten individually reviewed outputs; three template graphics; roles/logs; training; baseline and acceptance report; and two in-scope revision rounds. Delivery is 14 days after complete inputs. Maintenance begins the next month at 6,800/month: three seats, 30 bounded drafts, ten graphics, 100 retrievals, eight operations hours and four professional sampling/issue hours. Customers retain final per-item review; quote excess work.</p>\n<p>Price the implementation, evidence and collaboration process, not a model interface alone. Qualify only customers with measurable labor/vendor-replacement value supporting 6,800/month. At an actual customer rate of 150/hour, at least 45.34 hours/month must be saved, or other evidenced replacement value supplied. Do not invent incremental sales to justify the price.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":5,"title":"Market sizing & evidence","lead":"Build 400 qualified purchasing prospects toward 12 implementations, rather than applying a price to all hospitals.","body":"Sources: 80 introductions to verify, 200 public institution/brand prospects and 120 partner candidates. 60% substantive contact → 240; 25% completed meeting → 60; 20% purchase → 12. Record every stage. Hospital statistics are not the medical-aesthetics buyer count.\n\nPrioritize 5–20-person operations/content teams, multiple channels/products, a named reviewer, real tasks and budget. Segment TAM remains unknown. Deliver 2 / 4 / 6 implementations by month. Service starts the next month: 2 + 6 = eight customer-months; period-end six subscribers is an assumption. Month-three customers are not credited with future renewals.","sources":["S2"],"requirements":["R1"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Sources: 80 introductions to verify, 200 public institution/brand prospects and 120 partner candidates. 60% substantive contact → 240; 25% completed meeting → 60; 20% purchase → 12. Record every stage. Hospital statistics are not the medical-aesthetics buyer count.</p>\n<p>Prioritize 5–20-person operations/content teams, multiple channels/products, a named reviewer, real tasks and budget. Segment TAM remains unknown. Deliver 2 / 4 / 6 implementations by month. Service starts the next month: 2 + 6 = eight customer-months; period-end six subscribers is an assumption. Month-three customers are not credited with future renewals.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":6,"title":"Competition & alternatives","lead":"General tools already support workflows. We must demonstrate more reliable industry delivery and lower total effort.","body":"| Alternative | Public reference | Additional value to prove |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Dify | Annual Professional USD 590/workspace; Team USD 1,590; knowledge and workflow tools | Source preparation, review, task templates and service |\n| Coze | Subscription/credit tiers; individual, team and enterprise; notice of new-plan changes on November 12 | Traceable, acceptable outputs rather than an agent interface alone |\n| General model + human editor | A customer's current alternative | Better total time and fact checking, not just faster generation |\n| Agencies / custom developers | Existing delivery approaches; actual quotes to obtain | Scope, cost and repeatability |\n\n### Comparison design\nUse five real tasks with identical sources and objectives. Compare a general model plus documents against the proposed workflow. Where possible, blind the reviewer to the method. Record factual errors, source coverage, revision rounds and total labor. The knowledge base is a proposed asset, not an established moat.\n\n### Why a customer would buy\nCustomers may pay for dependable results and convenience without caring whether the software is called an agent. If an internal technical team can build more cheaply, acknowledge that the organization may not be a priority customer.","sources":["S6","S7"],"requirements":["R1","R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Alternative</th><th scope=\"col\">Public reference</th><th scope=\"col\">Additional value to prove</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dify</td><td>Annual Professional USD 590/workspace; Team USD 1,590; knowledge and workflow tools</td><td>Source preparation, review, task templates and service</td></tr><tr><td>Coze</td><td>Subscription/credit tiers; individual, team and enterprise; notice of new-plan changes on November 12</td><td>Traceable, acceptable outputs rather than an agent interface alone</td></tr><tr><td>General model + human editor</td><td>A customer&#x27;s current alternative</td><td>Better total time and fact checking, not just faster generation</td></tr><tr><td>Agencies / custom developers</td><td>Existing delivery approaches; actual quotes to obtain</td><td>Scope, cost and repeatability</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Comparison design</h3>\n<p>Use five real tasks with identical sources and objectives. Compare a general model plus documents against the proposed workflow. Where possible, blind the reviewer to the method. Record factual errors, source coverage, revision rounds and total labor. The knowledge base is a proposed asset, not an established moat.</p>\n<h3>Why a customer would buy</h3>\n<p>Customers may pay for dependable results and convenience without caring whether the software is called an agent. If an internal technical team can build more cheaply, acknowledge that the organization may not be a priority customer.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":7,"title":"Business model & pricing","lead":"Customers pay 19,800 for implementation and 6,800/month from the following month; pricing remains unvalidated.","body":"### Higher-value implementation\nCNY 19,800 per institution delivers one running source/content workflow: one brand/business line; at most 30 documents and 200 pages; versioned retrieval; ten individually reviewed outputs; three template graphics; roles/logs; training; baseline and acceptance report; and two in-scope revision rounds. Delivery is 14 days after complete inputs. Maintenance begins the next month at 6,800/month: three seats, 30 bounded drafts, ten graphics, 100 retrievals, eight operations hours and four professional sampling/issue hours. Customers retain final per-item review; quote excess work.\n\nPrice the implementation, evidence and collaboration process, not a model interface alone. Qualify only customers with measurable labor/vendor-replacement value supporting 6,800/month. At an actual customer rate of 150/hour, at least 45.34 hours/month must be saved, or other evidenced replacement value supplied. Do not invent incremental sales to justify the price.\n","sources":[],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Higher-value implementation</h3>\n<p>CNY 19,800 per institution delivers one running source/content workflow: one brand/business line; at most 30 documents and 200 pages; versioned retrieval; ten individually reviewed outputs; three template graphics; roles/logs; training; baseline and acceptance report; and two in-scope revision rounds. Delivery is 14 days after complete inputs. Maintenance begins the next month at 6,800/month: three seats, 30 bounded drafts, ten graphics, 100 retrievals, eight operations hours and four professional sampling/issue hours. Customers retain final per-item review; quote excess work.</p>\n<p>Price the implementation, evidence and collaboration process, not a model interface alone. Qualify only customers with measurable labor/vendor-replacement value supporting 6,800/month. At an actual customer rate of 150/hour, at least 45.34 hours/month must be saved, or other evidenced replacement value supplied. Do not invent incremental sales to justify the price.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":8,"title":"Unit economics & viability","lead":"Direct cost is CNY 4,800 per implementation and 1,800 per service month. Higher prices need customer value and delivery capacity.","body":"Implementation: 30 operations hours × 80 = 2,400; eight review hours × 150 = 1,200; models/deployment/design 1,200. Monthly service: eight operations hours × 80 + four review hours × 150 + 560 models/storage = 1,800. Reserve 8% of revenue for processing, taxes and refunds. Implementation contribution = 19,800 × 92% − 4,800 = 13,416; service contribution = 6,800 × 92% − 1,800 = 4,456.\n\nTarget common build 40,000 + operations 18,000 + sales 36,000 = 94,000. Twelve implementations and eight service months contribute 196,640, leaving 102,640. With no service sales, eight implementations cover 94,000. A 20% implementation discount reduces surplus by 43,718.40 to 58,921.60. Doubling implementation delivery cost reduces it by 57,600 to 45,040.","sources":[],"requirements":["R1","R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Implementation: 30 operations hours × 80 = 2,400; eight review hours × 150 = 1,200; models/deployment/design 1,200. Monthly service: eight operations hours × 80 + four review hours × 150 + 560 models/storage = 1,800. Reserve 8% of revenue for processing, taxes and refunds. Implementation contribution = 19,800 × 92% − 4,800 = 13,416; service contribution = 6,800 × 92% − 1,800 = 4,456.</p>\n<p>Target common build 40,000 + operations 18,000 + sales 36,000 = 94,000. Twelve implementations and eight service months contribute 196,640, leaving 102,640. With no service sales, eight implementations cover 94,000. A 20% implementation discount reduces surplus by 43,718.40 to 58,921.60. Doubling implementation delivery cost reduces it by 57,600 to 45,040.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":9,"title":"Acquiring the first customers","lead":"Twelve sales require 400 prospects and 60 completed meetings, with full selling cost included.","body":"400 → 240 substantive contacts → 60 completed needs meetings → 12 signed, paid implementations assumes 60% / 25% / 20%. In two weeks verify 60 prospects, complete 15 meetings and seek two kickoff payments. Source 80 introduction candidates, 200 public buyers and 120 partner candidates; none is a confirmed relationship yet.\n\nSales/marketing budget 36,000: 100 selling hours × 100 = 10,000; demos/samples 6,000; travel/events 8,000; partners 8,000; tools/contingency 4,000. Full CAC = 3,000 per implementation, already included. Allocate 30 hours to meetings, 40 to verification and 30 to proposals/follow-up. Revise if work exceeds this.\n\nDemonstrate one de-identified real task with sources, review, timing and permissions before a bounded 19,800 quote. No unsolicited bulk messaging; no outreach has been sent in this task.","sources":[],"requirements":["R3"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>400 → 240 substantive contacts → 60 completed needs meetings → 12 signed, paid implementations assumes 60% / 25% / 20%. In two weeks verify 60 prospects, complete 15 meetings and seek two kickoff payments. Source 80 introduction candidates, 200 public buyers and 120 partner candidates; none is a confirmed relationship yet.</p>\n<p>Sales/marketing budget 36,000: 100 selling hours × 100 = 10,000; demos/samples 6,000; travel/events 8,000; partners 8,000; tools/contingency 4,000. Full CAC = 3,000 per implementation, already included. Allocate 30 hours to meetings, 40 to verification and 30 to proposals/follow-up. Revise if work exceeds this.</p>\n<p>Demonstrate one de-identified real task with sources, review, timing and permissions before a bounded 19,800 quote. No unsolicited bulk messaging; no outreach has been sent in this task.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":10,"title":"Channels & sales process","lead":"Sell measurable workflow value, with payments at 40% / 40% / 20% milestones.","body":"Diagnosis → matched-task comparison → value calculation → scope/contract → 40% kickoff → 40% running workflow → 20% acceptance. Payments are 7,920 / 7,920 / 3,960 per sale; receipts do not establish fulfilled revenue. Recognize 19,800 in the modeled month only if delivery and acceptance are complete; otherwise defer.\n\nNew implementations: 2 / 4 / 6. Monthly service accounts: 0 / 2 / 6. Monthly revenue: 39,600 / 92,800 / 159,600, totaling 292,000. Six month-three service accounts assumes all six earlier customers renew; validate this rather than treating it as evidence. Partner compensation must fit the approved budget.","sources":[],"requirements":["R3"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Diagnosis → matched-task comparison → value calculation → scope/contract → 40% kickoff → 40% running workflow → 20% acceptance. Payments are 7,920 / 7,920 / 3,960 per sale; receipts do not establish fulfilled revenue. Recognize 19,800 in the modeled month only if delivery and acceptance are complete; otherwise defer.</p>\n<p>New implementations: 2 / 4 / 6. Monthly service accounts: 0 / 2 / 6. Monthly revenue: 39,600 / 92,800 / 159,600, totaling 292,000. Six month-three service accounts assumes all six earlier customers renew; validate this rather than treating it as evidence. Partner compensation must fit the approved budget.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":11,"title":"90-day economics & scale targets","lead":"The target is a six-figure CNY quarterly surplus; low sales can still produce a loss.","body":"| Scenario / stage | Paying customers | Revenue | Total budget | Target economic surplus |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Conservative | 4 | 92,800.00 | 108,224.00 | -15,424.00 |\n| Target | 12 | 292,000.00 | 189,360.00 | 102,640.00 |\n| Stretch | 20 | 504,800.00 | 289,184.00 | 215,616.00 |\n\n| Cost item | CNY budget |\n| --- | --- |\n| Implementation delivery | 57,600.00 |\n| Subscription delivery | 14,400.00 |\n| Processing and tax/refund reserve | 23,360.00 |\n| Sales and marketing | 36,000.00 |\n| Product build | 40,000.00 |\n| Operating labor and overhead | 18,000.00 |\n\n### Basis of calculation\nThis is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit.\n","sources":[],"requirements":["R1","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Scenario / stage</th><th scope=\"col\">Paying customers</th><th scope=\"col\">Revenue</th><th scope=\"col\">Total budget</th><th scope=\"col\">Target economic surplus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Conservative</td><td>4</td><td>92,800.00</td><td>108,224.00</td><td>-15,424.00</td></tr><tr><td>Target</td><td>12</td><td>292,000.00</td><td>189,360.00</td><td>102,640.00</td></tr><tr><td>Stretch</td><td>20</td><td>504,800.00</td><td>289,184.00</td><td>215,616.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cost item</th><th scope=\"col\">CNY budget</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Implementation delivery</td><td>57,600.00</td></tr><tr><td>Subscription delivery</td><td>14,400.00</td></tr><tr><td>Processing and tax/refund reserve</td><td>23,360.00</td></tr><tr><td>Sales and marketing</td><td>36,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Product build</td><td>40,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Operating labor and overhead</td><td>18,000.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Basis of calculation</h3>\n<p>This is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":12,"title":"Resources & cash planning","lead":"All build and operating costs are included: base budget CNY 189,360 versus 292,000 revenue.","body":"| Cost item | CNY budget |\n| --- | --- |\n| Implementation delivery | 57,600.00 |\n| Subscription delivery | 14,400.00 |\n| Processing and tax/refund reserve | 23,360.00 |\n| Sales and marketing | 36,000.00 |\n| Product build | 40,000.00 |\n| Operating labor and overhead | 18,000.00 |\n\nBuild 40,000 = 200 engineering hours × 150 + 125 product hours × 80. Common operations 18,000 are separate from client service labor. Twelve implementations require 456 direct hours; eight service months require 96: 552 total, plus 325 build hours, 100 sales hours and common operations. Assign at least two available delivery contributors and qualified review capacity; do not assume one person does everything.\n\nDiscuss 100,000 of working-capital funding, not an extra expense. Prepare a weekly ledger for receipts, reviewers/contractors and refund liabilities. Recalculate peak funding for delayed kickoff payments, acceptance or settlement. Release only 15,000 for the first 14 days, then expand against real orders.\n\n### Monthly funding illustration\n| Month | Fulfilled revenue | Economic spending | Cumulative balance |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 39,600 | 60,768 | -21,168 |\n| 2 | 92,800 | 58,224 | 13,408 |\n| 3 | 159,600 | 70,368 | 102,640 |\nAssumes all due sales settle in the same month and planned costs are paid. These month-end balances do not establish daily peak funding; deposits, holds, deferred delivery and taxes require an actual dated cash ledger. Working capital is financing, not an additional P&L cost.","sources":[],"requirements":["R1"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cost item</th><th scope=\"col\">CNY budget</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Implementation delivery</td><td>57,600.00</td></tr><tr><td>Subscription delivery</td><td>14,400.00</td></tr><tr><td>Processing and tax/refund reserve</td><td>23,360.00</td></tr><tr><td>Sales and marketing</td><td>36,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Product build</td><td>40,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Operating labor and overhead</td><td>18,000.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Build 40,000 = 200 engineering hours × 150 + 125 product hours × 80. Common operations 18,000 are separate from client service labor. Twelve implementations require 456 direct hours; eight service months require 96: 552 total, plus 325 build hours, 100 sales hours and common operations. Assign at least two available delivery contributors and qualified review capacity; do not assume one person does everything.</p>\n<p>Discuss 100,000 of working-capital funding, not an extra expense. Prepare a weekly ledger for receipts, reviewers/contractors and refund liabilities. Recalculate peak funding for delayed kickoff payments, acceptance or settlement. Release only 15,000 for the first 14 days, then expand against real orders.</p>\n<h3>Monthly funding illustration</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Month</th><th scope=\"col\">Fulfilled revenue</th><th scope=\"col\">Economic spending</th><th scope=\"col\">Cumulative balance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>39,600</td><td>60,768</td><td>-21,168</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>92,800</td><td>58,224</td><td>13,408</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>159,600</td><td>70,368</td><td>102,640</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Assumes all due sales settle in the same month and planned costs are paid. These month-end balances do not establish daily peak funding; deposits, holds, deferred delivery and taxes require an actual dated cash ledger. Working capital is financing, not an additional P&amp;L cost.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":13,"title":"90-day milestones","lead":"Deliver 2 / 4 / 6 implementations, expanding only with quality and payment evidence.","body":"D7: prospect pool, five interviews, reviewer and sample. D14: 15 needs meetings, five matched tasks, seek two kickoff receipts of 7,920. D30: accept two implementations. D60: accept four more, with the prior two on service. D90: accept six more, with six earlier customers on service; reconcile 292,000 revenue and 102,640 target surplus.\n\nIf none of the first 15 qualified meetings accepts the price or demonstrates ROI, revise audience and scope. Delayed acceptance defers revenue and surplus; signed intent is not current fulfilled sales.","sources":[],"requirements":["R3","R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>D7: prospect pool, five interviews, reviewer and sample. D14: 15 needs meetings, five matched tasks, seek two kickoff receipts of 7,920. D30: accept two implementations. D60: accept four more, with the prior two on service. D90: accept six more, with six earlier customers on service; reconcile 292,000 revenue and 102,640 target surplus.</p>\n<p>If none of the first 15 qualified meetings accepts the price or demonstrates ROI, revise audience and scope. Delayed acceptance defers revenue and surplus; signed intent is not current fulfilled sales.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":14,"title":"Metrics & acceptance criteria","lead":"Assess payment, fulfillment, cost and quality together rather than revenue alone.","body":"12 accepted implementations; eight service months; ≥30% total time saved; zero unresolved critical factual errors; full CAC ≤3,000; budget ≤189,360.\n\nThese are proposed thresholds. Count unique valid payers, remove invalid/refunded transactions, and accept only usable confirmed outputs. Separate mature observation periods. Track source, reach, unique visits, actual payment, delivery, refunds and full cost. Downloads and intent are not revenue. Pause expansion and revise the plan if early pricing, quality or unit-cost gates fail.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>12 accepted implementations; eight service months; ≥30% total time saved; zero unresolved critical factual errors; full CAC ≤3,000; budget ≤189,360.</p>\n<p>These are proposed thresholds. Count unique valid payers, remove invalid/refunded transactions, and accept only usable confirmed outputs. Separate mature observation periods. Track source, reach, unique visits, actual payment, delivery, refunds and full cost. Downloads and intent are not revenue. Pause expansion and revise the plan if early pricing, quality or unit-cost gates fail.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":15,"title":"Risks & responses","lead":"Industry errors and uncontrolled human service effort matter more than the ability to generate text.","body":"| Risk | Early signal | Response / owner |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Incorrect or stale sources | Confused model/version; citation fails to support a claim | Engineering preserves versions; reviewer checks; stop generation when evidence is inadequate |\n| Advertising / clinical boundaries | Efficacy guarantees or unverified applicability | Customer and reviewer confirm intended use; no automatic publishing |\n| Uncontrolled labor | First three pilots repeatedly exceed 48 hours | I narrow scope, reprice or pause productization |\n| Weak renewal | Value below 6,800 or no recurring task | Reassess actual ROI; no unlimited support sustained by discounts |\n| Low sales efficiency | Fewer than two willing payers after 20 qualified interviews | Narrow the audience or stop before building a platform |\n| Failed data separation | Cross-customer retrieval or unclear permission | Engineering suspends affected access and investigates scope |\n\n### Professional checking is not administrative approval\nThe operating business must verify publication eligibility and applicable review requirements. Software supports provenance, review and records. My industry experience does not replace all professional verification of product facts.\n\n### Accountability\nI own customer scope; engineering owns permission and logs; the reviewer checks facts; the customer owns final use and publication decisions. Agree fees, permissions and integration boundaries before contracting.","sources":["S10","S11"],"requirements":["R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Risk</th><th scope=\"col\">Early signal</th><th scope=\"col\">Response / owner</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Incorrect or stale sources</td><td>Confused model/version; citation fails to support a claim</td><td>Engineering preserves versions; reviewer checks; stop generation when evidence is inadequate</td></tr><tr><td>Advertising / clinical boundaries</td><td>Efficacy guarantees or unverified applicability</td><td>Customer and reviewer confirm intended use; no automatic publishing</td></tr><tr><td>Uncontrolled labor</td><td>First three pilots repeatedly exceed 48 hours</td><td>I narrow scope, reprice or pause productization</td></tr><tr><td>Weak renewal</td><td>Value below 6,800 or no recurring task</td><td>Reassess actual ROI; no unlimited support sustained by discounts</td></tr><tr><td>Low sales efficiency</td><td>Fewer than two willing payers after 20 qualified interviews</td><td>Narrow the audience or stop before building a platform</td></tr><tr><td>Failed data separation</td><td>Cross-customer retrieval or unclear permission</td><td>Engineering suspends affected access and investigates scope</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Professional checking is not administrative approval</h3>\n<p>The operating business must verify publication eligibility and applicable review requirements. Software supports provenance, review and records. My industry experience does not replace all professional verification of product facts.</p>\n<h3>Accountability</h3>\n<p>I own customer scope; engineering owns permission and logs; the reviewer checks facts; the customer owns final use and publication decisions. Agree fees, permissions and integration boundaries before contracting.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":16,"title":"Team roles & collaboration","lead":"I will lead product and market execution, while assessing technical choices and resources jointly with the team.","body":"### My proposed responsibilities\nI will own industry customers, source/content standards, quotation scope, sales and delivery reviews. I can rapidly prototype and prepare experiments with AI, and want to assess reliability, costs and scalable implementation with engineering. A prototype is not proof of production-service readiness.\n\n| Role | Proposed responsibility | To confirm |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 最高 | Product, customers/users, market work, experiments and review | Availability and stage targets |\n| Engineering lead | Architecture, models/tools, permissions, tasks and cost logs | People, hours, schedule and maintenance |\n| Professional / content reviewer | Facts, asset rights and output quality | Reviewer, competence, price and scope |\n| Customer / user | Usable material, confirmation, feedback and acceptance | Consent and intended use |\n| Team247 lead | Budget, resources, payment/contract entity and stage decisions | Authority and available resources |\n\n### Decisions to make together\nLaunch platform, core tasks, models/tools, usage budget, data handling, release requirements, price, responsibilities and acceptance. Joint discussion is not an excuse to provide no proposal: this BP offers comparable assumptions and experiments for the team to revise.\n\n### Working cadence\nReview real activations/customers, payments/refunds, output quality, effort/API costs and next-week decisions weekly. Record a continue/adjust/pause decision at days 14 and 30. These are proposals, not staffing or budget commitments already obtained.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>My proposed responsibilities</h3>\n<p>I will own industry customers, source/content standards, quotation scope, sales and delivery reviews. I can rapidly prototype and prepare experiments with AI, and want to assess reliability, costs and scalable implementation with engineering. A prototype is not proof of production-service readiness.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Role</th><th scope=\"col\">Proposed responsibility</th><th scope=\"col\">To confirm</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>最高</td><td>Product, customers/users, market work, experiments and review</td><td>Availability and stage targets</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering lead</td><td>Architecture, models/tools, permissions, tasks and cost logs</td><td>People, hours, schedule and maintenance</td></tr><tr><td>Professional / content reviewer</td><td>Facts, asset rights and output quality</td><td>Reviewer, competence, price and scope</td></tr><tr><td>Customer / user</td><td>Usable material, confirmation, feedback and acceptance</td><td>Consent and intended use</td></tr><tr><td>Team247 lead</td><td>Budget, resources, payment/contract entity and stage decisions</td><td>Authority and available resources</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Decisions to make together</h3>\n<p>Launch platform, core tasks, models/tools, usage budget, data handling, release requirements, price, responsibilities and acceptance. Joint discussion is not an excuse to provide no proposal: this BP offers comparable assumptions and experiments for the team to revise.</p>\n<h3>Working cadence</h3>\n<p>Review real activations/customers, payments/refunds, output quality, effort/API costs and next-week decisions weekly. Record a continue/adjust/pause decision at days 14 and 30. These are proposals, not staffing or budget commitments already obtained.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":17,"title":"Evidence, assumptions & unknowns","lead":"Public sources support context and constraints. Project revenue and growth remain unverified assumptions.","body":"| Evidence | Date and limits |\n| --- | --- |\n| [S2 · National Health Commission: 2024 statistical bulletin](https://www.nhc.gov.cn/guihuaxxs/c100132/202512/9db8db5488a748c4b1e1068a4a8c4455.shtml?menuid=128) | Published December 2025; year-end 2024 statistics. 38,710 total hospitals and 26,956 private hospitals. These are not medical-aesthetics institution counts. |\n| [S6 · Dify official pricing](https://dify.ai/pricing) | Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09. Annual Professional USD 590/workspace and Team USD 1,590. These are not the total cost of an industry service. |\n| [S7 · Coze official plans and pricing](https://docs.coze.cn/cozespace_coze_billing_overview) | Checked 2026-11-09; page announces changes on November 12. Subscriptions and credits. Near-term price changes mean these are not a fixed long-term API cost. |\n| [S10 · Medical-aesthetics advertising enforcement guidance](https://www.samr.gov.cn/zw/zfxxgk/fdzdgknr/ggjgs/art/2023/art_d1b46dbc27214abcace53a0ec539f7bb.html) | 2021 guidance; migrated official page. Qualifications, review and content restrictions. Human checking is not regulatory approval. |\n| [S11 · Medical advertising supervision guidance](https://www.samr.gov.cn/zw/zfxxgk/fdzdgknr/ggjgs/art/2025/art_cd56662cf13b4ad59eabfe31cb1122e1.html) | Published May 2025. Informs advertising-review boundaries; it is not a compliance determination for this product. |\n\n### Critical gaps\nA real 200-prospect list; professional review capacity; current customer effort and budgets; actual payments/renewals; API/deployment quotations; repeatable delivery effort.\n\n### Replace assumptions with evidence\nUse sourced prospect records, interviews, payment/refund records, task logs, supplier invoices and mature-cohort observations. Mark missing evidence as unverified; do not invent customers, case-study revenue, permissions or testimonials.\n\n### Evidence levels\nPublic facts retain their sources and dates. Prices, counts and costs are planning assumptions. Formula outputs are calculations. Relationships, resources and technical capability remain to be validated. Recheck dynamic prices before launch. The BP and website are deliverables; commercial viability has not been established.\n\nNew target gaps: accepted quotations, attributable reach, actual payment/refunds, full labor/API costs, delivery capacity and team resources. Page 11 economics V7 supersedes earlier figures; public sources do not establish project sales.","sources":["S2","S6","S7","S10","S11"],"requirements":["R1","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Evidence</th><th scope=\"col\">Date and limits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.nhc.gov.cn/guihuaxxs/c100132/202512/9db8db5488a748c4b1e1068a4a8c4455.shtml?menuid=128\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S2 · National Health Commission: 2024 statistical bulletin</a></td><td>Published December 2025; year-end 2024 statistics. 38,710 total hospitals and 26,956 private hospitals. These are not medical-aesthetics institution counts.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://dify.ai/pricing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S6 · Dify official pricing</a></td><td>Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09. Annual Professional USD 590/workspace and Team USD 1,590. These are not the total cost of an industry service.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://docs.coze.cn/cozespace_coze_billing_overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S7 · Coze official plans and pricing</a></td><td>Checked 2026-11-09; page announces changes on November 12. Subscriptions and credits. Near-term price changes mean these are not a fixed long-term API cost.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.samr.gov.cn/zw/zfxxgk/fdzdgknr/ggjgs/art/2023/art_d1b46dbc27214abcace53a0ec539f7bb.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S10 · Medical-aesthetics advertising enforcement guidance</a></td><td>2021 guidance; migrated official page. Qualifications, review and content restrictions. Human checking is not regulatory approval.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.samr.gov.cn/zw/zfxxgk/fdzdgknr/ggjgs/art/2025/art_cd56662cf13b4ad59eabfe31cb1122e1.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S11 · Medical advertising supervision guidance</a></td><td>Published May 2025. Informs advertising-review boundaries; it is not a compliance determination for this product.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Critical gaps</h3>\n<p>A real 200-prospect list; professional review capacity; current customer effort and budgets; actual payments/renewals; API/deployment quotations; repeatable delivery effort.</p>\n<h3>Replace assumptions with evidence</h3>\n<p>Use sourced prospect records, interviews, payment/refund records, task logs, supplier invoices and mature-cohort observations. Mark missing evidence as unverified; do not invent customers, case-study revenue, permissions or testimonials.</p>\n<h3>Evidence levels</h3>\n<p>Public facts retain their sources and dates. Prices, counts and costs are planning assumptions. Formula outputs are calculations. Relationships, resources and technical capability remain to be validated. Recheck dynamic prices before launch. The BP and website are deliverables; commercial viability has not been established.</p>\n<p>New target gaps: accepted quotations, attributable reach, actual payment/refunds, full labor/API costs, delivery capacity and team resources. Page 11 economics V7 supersedes earlier figures; public sources do not establish project sales.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":18,"title":"Recommendation & decisions","lead":"Organize resources around the larger commercial objective; target economic surplus of CNY 102,640.00 requires its assumptions to hold.","body":"Position 19,800 implementation plus 6,800 monthly service for higher-value buyers. Secure two kickoff payments and evidenced ROI before scaling to 12 implementations/eight service months.\n\nConfirm owners, available labor, technical route, budget, operating/tax entity, channels and stop gates together. I will drive product, market, content and validation. These are the business outcomes to pursue; orders, reach and costs still require evidence. Recalculate actual results when targets are missed rather than promising profit.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Position 19,800 implementation plus 6,800 monthly service for higher-value buyers. Secure two kickoff payments and evidenced ROI before scaling to 12 implementations/eight service months.</p>\n<p>Confirm owners, available labor, technical route, budget, operating/tax entity, channels and stop gates together. I will drive product, market, content and validation. These are the business outcomes to pursue; orders, reach and costs still require evidence. Recalculate actual results when targets are missed rather than promising profit.</p>","appendixHtml":""}]},{"id":"story","number":"03","name":"Personal-story visual novels","position":"Turn lived experiences into complete, playable stories","pages":[{"number":1,"title":"Executive summary","lead":"Target 1,000 paid authors in 90 days, CNY 299,000 revenue and 108,080 economic surplus.","body":"### Tiered works and prices\nStandard CNY 199/work: 3,000–5,000 Chinese characters across branches, three characters, six image assets, three endings, one in-scope revision, 30-day hosting and local export. Polished CNY 699/work: the same technical baseline plus interview/character work and at most 90 minutes of editing, up to 12 assets and two consolidated revisions. Quote long-form and voice separately; no unlimited edits.\n\nThe free entry is a playable template sample and lightweight preview, replacing a free fully customized work for everyone. Disclose scope before payment. Authors pay; friends play free. Verify source rights, default to private and allow sharing withdrawal. Target mix: 80% standard / 20% polished, giving CNY 299 average order value. The mix is untested; players are not paying authors.\n","sources":[],"requirements":["R4","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Tiered works and prices</h3>\n<p>Standard CNY 199/work: 3,000–5,000 Chinese characters across branches, three characters, six image assets, three endings, one in-scope revision, 30-day hosting and local export. Polished CNY 699/work: the same technical baseline plus interview/character work and at most 90 minutes of editing, up to 12 assets and two consolidated revisions. Quote long-form and voice separately; no unlimited edits.</p>\n<p>The free entry is a playable template sample and lightweight preview, replacing a free fully customized work for everyone. Disclose scope before payment. Authors pay; friends play free. Verify source rights, default to private and allow sharing withdrawal. Target mix: 80% standard / 20% polished, giving CNY 299 average order value. The mix is untested; players are not paying authors.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":2,"title":"Customers & the problem","lead":"Authors and players are distinct roles. Being moved by a story does not prove willingness to create or pay.","body":"| Role | Demand hypothesis | Behavior to validate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Author | Wants personal experience turned into a story with choices | Supplies usable material and confirms characters, outline and facts |\n| Payer | Purchases a more complete or personalized finished work | Pays after seeing real examples and specifications |\n| Player | Enters a friend's story through a link | Starts, reaches an ending and decides whether to create |\n| Third party depicted | May have their likeness or experiences used | Required permission, deletion and withdrawal from public sharing |\n\n### Initial segment\nTest adult graduation, friendship, career-transition and commemorative stories first. Users need not know scriptwriting or game tools, but must verify people and events. Breakup stories may be researched without claiming therapy or prediction of real people's reactions.\n\n### Behavioral questions\nUse a piece of material the user has permission to supply. Observe whether they play through, whom they would show it to, and whether they have another story. Record why people refuse upload or sharing; do not interview only enthusiastic respondents.","sources":[],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Role</th><th scope=\"col\">Demand hypothesis</th><th scope=\"col\">Behavior to validate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Author</td><td>Wants personal experience turned into a story with choices</td><td>Supplies usable material and confirms characters, outline and facts</td></tr><tr><td>Payer</td><td>Purchases a more complete or personalized finished work</td><td>Pays after seeing real examples and specifications</td></tr><tr><td>Player</td><td>Enters a friend&#x27;s story through a link</td><td>Starts, reaches an ending and decides whether to create</td></tr><tr><td>Third party depicted</td><td>May have their likeness or experiences used</td><td>Required permission, deletion and withdrawal from public sharing</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Initial segment</h3>\n<p>Test adult graduation, friendship, career-transition and commemorative stories first. Users need not know scriptwriting or game tools, but must verify people and events. Breakup stories may be researched without claiming therapy or prediction of real people&#x27;s reactions.</p>\n<h3>Behavioral questions</h3>\n<p>Use a piece of material the user has permission to supply. Observe whether they play through, whom they would show it to, and whether they have another story. Record why people refuse upload or sharing; do not interview only enthusiastic respondents.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":3,"title":"Product & user journey","lead":"Confirm source events and invented branches separately before producing a complete playable story.","body":"Start with adults recording graduation, friendship or career transitions. Anniversary gifts are a testable use case; third-party private information without appropriate consent is not a source. Breakup or traumatic experiences may represent demand, but this trial promises neither therapy nor prediction of another person's reactions.\n\nText or voice input → extract characters, events and chronology → author confirms fact versus fictional branch → generate and approve outline → generate text and images → check reachable branches and character consistency → review where necessary → private work link → author plays through → author chooses whether to share. Before importing chats, remove names, contact details and irrelevant third-party content. Default to private, without training use.\n\nExample: “Turn my transition from leaving a job to winning my first independent contract into a story with three choices.” Confirm which events happened and which alternatives are imagined. AI-written dialogue must not be presented as a real person's original conversation.","sources":[],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Start with adults recording graduation, friendship or career transitions. Anniversary gifts are a testable use case; third-party private information without appropriate consent is not a source. Breakup or traumatic experiences may represent demand, but this trial promises neither therapy nor prediction of another person&#x27;s reactions.</p>\n<p>Text or voice input → extract characters, events and chronology → author confirms fact versus fictional branch → generate and approve outline → generate text and images → check reachable branches and character consistency → review where necessary → private work link → author plays through → author chooses whether to share. Before importing chats, remove names, contact details and irrelevant third-party content. Default to private, without training use.</p>\n<p>Example: “Turn my transition from leaving a job to winning my first independent contract into a story with three choices.” Confirm which events happened and which alternatives are imagined. AI-written dialogue must not be presented as a real person&#x27;s original conversation.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":4,"title":"MVP & delivery scope","lead":"Raise order value through defined delivery tiers; validate sample quality before automation promises.","body":"### Tiered works and prices\nStandard CNY 199/work: 3,000–5,000 Chinese characters across branches, three characters, six image assets, three endings, one in-scope revision, 30-day hosting and local export. Polished CNY 699/work: the same technical baseline plus interview/character work and at most 90 minutes of editing, up to 12 assets and two consolidated revisions. Quote long-form and voice separately; no unlimited edits.\n\nThe free entry is a playable template sample and lightweight preview, replacing a free fully customized work for everyone. Disclose scope before payment. Authors pay; friends play free. Verify source rights, default to private and allow sharing withdrawal. Target mix: 80% standard / 20% polished, giving CNY 299 average order value. The mix is untested; players are not paying authors.\n","sources":[],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Tiered works and prices</h3>\n<p>Standard CNY 199/work: 3,000–5,000 Chinese characters across branches, three characters, six image assets, three endings, one in-scope revision, 30-day hosting and local export. Polished CNY 699/work: the same technical baseline plus interview/character work and at most 90 minutes of editing, up to 12 assets and two consolidated revisions. Quote long-form and voice separately; no unlimited edits.</p>\n<p>The free entry is a playable template sample and lightweight preview, replacing a free fully customized work for everyone. Disclose scope before payment. Authors pay; friends play free. Verify source rights, default to private and allow sharing withdrawal. Target mix: 80% standard / 20% polished, giving CNY 299 average order value. The mix is untested; players are not paying authors.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":5,"title":"Market sizing & evidence","lead":"Expand from a 100-author test to 1,000 paid authors, with 3,000 stretch.","body":"Target funnel: 50,000 unique visits → 10,000 completed previews/plays (20%) → 1,000 paid authors (10%). Count one initial order each; no repeat purchase is needed to reach the target. Stretch requires 150,000 visits, 30,000 previews and 3,000 payers with a larger budget.\n\nStart with adult graduation, birthday/anniversary, friendship and career stories using authorized material. Do not market therapy or life prediction. Later 10,000/100,000 paid-author stages depend on measured acquisition and automated delivery; player views are not payers.","sources":["S1"],"requirements":["R1"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Target funnel: 50,000 unique visits → 10,000 completed previews/plays (20%) → 1,000 paid authors (10%). Count one initial order each; no repeat purchase is needed to reach the target. Stretch requires 150,000 visits, 30,000 previews and 3,000 payers with a larger budget.</p>\n<p>Start with adult graduation, birthday/anniversary, friendship and career stories using authorized material. Do not market therapy or life prediction. Later 10,000/100,000 paid-author stages depend on measured acquisition and automated delivery; player views are not payers.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":6,"title":"Competition & alternatives","lead":"The advantage must come from complete production and personal expression, not simply generating more words.","body":"| Alternative | Capability / reference price | Difference to validate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| AI Dungeon | Journey USD 14.99/month; interactive narrative and model allowances | Personal material, consistent characters, a defined finished work and sharing |\n| Ren'Py | Open-source visual-novel engine, free for commercial use | Ordinary users avoid learning scripts, asset assembly and branching |\n| Writing models + image tools | Users can combine tools themselves | Less switching and rework; a complete experience |\n| Human-made commemorative work | High-touch personal expression; actual quotes unverified | Automation reduces cost while preserving personal meaning |\n\n### Comparison task\nUse the same authorized personal material with a tool combination and the proposed workflow. Record completion time, learning steps, character errors, image rework, reachable endings and actual willingness to pay.\n\n### If the platform hypothesis fails\nIf purchases occur mainly on anniversaries, consider a small curated service rather than forcing a high-frequency platform narrative. Completion matters more than total length; a 30,000-character branching script does not mean every player reads 30,000 characters.","sources":["S8","S9"],"requirements":["R1","R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Alternative</th><th scope=\"col\">Capability / reference price</th><th scope=\"col\">Difference to validate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>AI Dungeon</td><td>Journey USD 14.99/month; interactive narrative and model allowances</td><td>Personal material, consistent characters, a defined finished work and sharing</td></tr><tr><td>Ren&#x27;Py</td><td>Open-source visual-novel engine, free for commercial use</td><td>Ordinary users avoid learning scripts, asset assembly and branching</td></tr><tr><td>Writing models + image tools</td><td>Users can combine tools themselves</td><td>Less switching and rework; a complete experience</td></tr><tr><td>Human-made commemorative work</td><td>High-touch personal expression; actual quotes unverified</td><td>Automation reduces cost while preserving personal meaning</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Comparison task</h3>\n<p>Use the same authorized personal material with a tool combination and the proposed workflow. Record completion time, learning steps, character errors, image rework, reachable endings and actual willingness to pay.</p>\n<h3>If the platform hypothesis fails</h3>\n<p>If purchases occur mainly on anniversaries, consider a small curated service rather than forcing a high-frequency platform narrative. Completion matters more than total length; a 30,000-character branching script does not mean every player reads 30,000 characters.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":7,"title":"Business model & pricing","lead":"CNY 199 standard + 699 polished, targeting CNY 299 average order value.","body":"### Tiered works and prices\nStandard CNY 199/work: 3,000–5,000 Chinese characters across branches, three characters, six image assets, three endings, one in-scope revision, 30-day hosting and local export. Polished CNY 699/work: the same technical baseline plus interview/character work and at most 90 minutes of editing, up to 12 assets and two consolidated revisions. Quote long-form and voice separately; no unlimited edits.\n\nThe free entry is a playable template sample and lightweight preview, replacing a free fully customized work for everyone. Disclose scope before payment. Authors pay; friends play free. Verify source rights, default to private and allow sharing withdrawal. Target mix: 80% standard / 20% polished, giving CNY 299 average order value. The mix is untested; players are not paying authors.\n","sources":[],"requirements":["R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>Tiered works and prices</h3>\n<p>Standard CNY 199/work: 3,000–5,000 Chinese characters across branches, three characters, six image assets, three endings, one in-scope revision, 30-day hosting and local export. Polished CNY 699/work: the same technical baseline plus interview/character work and at most 90 minutes of editing, up to 12 assets and two consolidated revisions. Quote long-form and voice separately; no unlimited edits.</p>\n<p>The free entry is a playable template sample and lightweight preview, replacing a free fully customized work for everyone. Disclose scope before payment. Authors pay; friends play free. Verify source rights, default to private and allow sharing withdrawal. Target mix: 80% standard / 20% polished, giving CNY 299 average order value. The mix is untested; players are not paying authors.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":8,"title":"Unit economics & viability","lead":"At CNY 299 blended order value and 80 fulfillment cost, contribution after reserves is 195.08/order.","body":"Standard direct cost 45: models/images 15, storage/export 5, review/support 25. Polished 220: generation/assets 30, storage 10, editing/review/support 180. Weighted cost = 80% × 45 + 20% × 220 = 80. Reserve 8% for processing, tax and refunds: 299 × 92% − 80 = 195.08. Labor budgets require about 15 minutes per standard work and 90-minute polished editing plus review; log actual effort.\n\n10,000 free previews × 0.20 = 2,000, not 10,000 custom long works. Build 30,000 + operations 15,000 + marketing 40,000 + previews 2,000 = 87,000. Break-even rounds up to 446 mixed orders. If all 1,000 buy only standard: revenue 199,000, delivery 45,000, reserve 15,920, other costs 87,000, surplus 51,080. At 150 average fulfillment cost, mixed-case surplus falls to 38,080.","sources":[],"requirements":["R1","R2"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Standard direct cost 45: models/images 15, storage/export 5, review/support 25. Polished 220: generation/assets 30, storage 10, editing/review/support 180. Weighted cost = 80% × 45 + 20% × 220 = 80. Reserve 8% for processing, tax and refunds: 299 × 92% − 80 = 195.08. Labor budgets require about 15 minutes per standard work and 90-minute polished editing plus review; log actual effort.</p>\n<p>10,000 free previews × 0.20 = 2,000, not 10,000 custom long works. Build 30,000 + operations 15,000 + marketing 40,000 + previews 2,000 = 87,000. Break-even rounds up to 446 mixed orders. If all 1,000 buy only standard: revenue 199,000, delivery 45,000, reserve 15,920, other costs 87,000, surplus 51,080. At 150 average fulfillment cost, mixed-case surplus falls to 38,080.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":9,"title":"Acquiring the first customers","lead":"Budget CNY 40,000 to acquire 1,000 paid authors: full CAC target 40.","body":"Thirty creator/community entries × 1,000 unique visits = 30,000; 20 playable cases × 500 = 10,000; author sharing, search and direct recruitment 10,000. Deduplicate sources before attribution. The partner funnel, 100 candidates → 60 substantive discussions → 30 agreements, is unverified.\n\nMarketing 40,000 includes partnerships/ads 18,000; content/sample labor 10,000; demo assets 4,000; research/attribution 4,000; sharing credits 4,000. Actual redeemed credits reduce revenue; the model reserves an equivalent acquisition cost, without double counting or treating credits as income. Cash commissions must also fit the cap. Obtain permission to display cases.\n\nTest each channel with two real examples. Track visits, completed previews, purchases, refunds and order value. Stop expansion if CAC exceeds 80 without compensating economics. Secure 100 paid authors before expanding toward 1,000.","sources":[],"requirements":["R3"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Thirty creator/community entries × 1,000 unique visits = 30,000; 20 playable cases × 500 = 10,000; author sharing, search and direct recruitment 10,000. Deduplicate sources before attribution. The partner funnel, 100 candidates → 60 substantive discussions → 30 agreements, is unverified.</p>\n<p>Marketing 40,000 includes partnerships/ads 18,000; content/sample labor 10,000; demo assets 4,000; research/attribution 4,000; sharing credits 4,000. Actual redeemed credits reduce revenue; the model reserves an equivalent acquisition cost, without double counting or treating credits as income. Cash commissions must also fit the cap. Obtain permission to display cases.</p>\n<p>Test each channel with two real examples. Track visits, completed previews, purchases, refunds and order value. Stop expansion if CAC exceeds 80 without compensating economics. Secure 100 paid authors before expanding toward 1,000.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":10,"title":"Channels & sales process","lead":"Sell through a complete playable sample, clear specifications and word of mouth.","body":"Demonstrate a choice → play a template → submit authorized story material → review 199/699 scope and delivery dates → pay → confirm outline → produce/accept → private link with revocable sharing. Award sharing credits only for valid, non-refunded new payments, within a 4,000 cap. Clicks, player views and multiple commission levels are not revenue.\n\nDeliver 100 / 300 / 600 orders by month, with revenue 29,900 / 89,700 / 179,400 at the 80/20 mix. Cap orders and display queues when capacity is full. Undelivered receipts remain liabilities rather than current revenue. Proposed delivery is 48 hours standard and five working days polished, subject to trial evidence.","sources":[],"requirements":["R3"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Demonstrate a choice → play a template → submit authorized story material → review 199/699 scope and delivery dates → pay → confirm outline → produce/accept → private link with revocable sharing. Award sharing credits only for valid, non-refunded new payments, within a 4,000 cap. Clicks, player views and multiple commission levels are not revenue.</p>\n<p>Deliver 100 / 300 / 600 orders by month, with revenue 29,900 / 89,700 / 179,400 at the 80/20 mix. Cap orders and display queues when capacity is full. Undelivered receipts remain liabilities rather than current revenue. Proposed delivery is 48 hours standard and five working days polished, subject to trial evidence.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":11,"title":"90-day economics & scale targets","lead":"Scale and order value jointly support the target; the conservative case shows the effect of weak sales.","body":"| Scenario / stage | Paying customers | Revenue | Total budget | Target economic surplus |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Conservative | 200 | 59,800.00 | 86,784.00 | -26,984.00 |\n| Target | 1,000 | 299,000.00 | 190,920.00 | 108,080.00 |\n| Stretch | 3,000 | 897,000.00 | 477,760.00 | 419,240.00 |\n\n| Cost item | CNY budget |\n| --- | --- |\n| Paid-work delivery | 80,000.00 |\n| Processing and tax/refund reserve | 23,920.00 |\n| Marketing | 40,000.00 |\n| Free samples | 2,000.00 |\n| Product build | 30,000.00 |\n| Operating labor and overhead | 15,000.00 |\n\n### Basis of calculation\nThis is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit.\n","sources":[],"requirements":["R1","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Scenario / stage</th><th scope=\"col\">Paying customers</th><th scope=\"col\">Revenue</th><th scope=\"col\">Total budget</th><th scope=\"col\">Target economic surplus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Conservative</td><td>200</td><td>59,800.00</td><td>86,784.00</td><td>-26,984.00</td></tr><tr><td>Target</td><td>1,000</td><td>299,000.00</td><td>190,920.00</td><td>108,080.00</td></tr><tr><td>Stretch</td><td>3,000</td><td>897,000.00</td><td>477,760.00</td><td>419,240.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cost item</th><th scope=\"col\">CNY budget</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paid-work delivery</td><td>80,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Processing and tax/refund reserve</td><td>23,920.00</td></tr><tr><td>Marketing</td><td>40,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Free samples</td><td>2,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Product build</td><td>30,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Operating labor and overhead</td><td>15,000.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Basis of calculation</h3>\n<p>This is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":12,"title":"Resources & cash planning","lead":"The CNY 190,920 target budget includes paid fulfillment, free previews, all marketing and build.","body":"| Cost item | CNY budget |\n| --- | --- |\n| Paid-work delivery | 80,000.00 |\n| Processing and tax/refund reserve | 23,920.00 |\n| Marketing | 40,000.00 |\n| Free samples | 2,000.00 |\n| Product build | 30,000.00 |\n| Operating labor and overhead | 15,000.00 |\n\nBuild 30,000 = 160 engineering hours × 150 + 75 product hours × 80. Eight hundred standard works × 15 minutes = 200 hours; 200 polished works × 90 minutes = 300 editing hours, plus about 100 polished-review hours: roughly 600 production/review hours. Month three needs about 360 hours for 600 orders: at least three collaborators each supplying 120 hours, funded within delivery costs. Confirm actual people and rates. A 3,000-order stretch needs additional capacity.\n\nDiscuss 80,000 working capital; release 10,000 for ten quality samples and a 100-order conversion test first. Expand marketing after sales evidence, retaining funding for fulfillment and refunds.\n\n### Monthly funding illustration\n| Month | Fulfilled revenue | Economic spending | Cumulative balance |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 29,900 | 45,792 | -15,892 |\n| 2 | 89,700 | 58,776 | 15,032 |\n| 3 | 179,400 | 86,352 | 108,080 |\nAssumes all due sales settle in the same month and planned costs are paid. These month-end balances do not establish daily peak funding; deposits, holds, deferred delivery and taxes require an actual dated cash ledger. Working capital is financing, not an additional P&L cost.","sources":[],"requirements":["R1"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cost item</th><th scope=\"col\">CNY budget</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paid-work delivery</td><td>80,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Processing and tax/refund reserve</td><td>23,920.00</td></tr><tr><td>Marketing</td><td>40,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Free samples</td><td>2,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Product build</td><td>30,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Operating labor and overhead</td><td>15,000.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Build 30,000 = 160 engineering hours × 150 + 75 product hours × 80. Eight hundred standard works × 15 minutes = 200 hours; 200 polished works × 90 minutes = 300 editing hours, plus about 100 polished-review hours: roughly 600 production/review hours. Month three needs about 360 hours for 600 orders: at least three collaborators each supplying 120 hours, funded within delivery costs. Confirm actual people and rates. A 3,000-order stretch needs additional capacity.</p>\n<p>Discuss 80,000 working capital; release 10,000 for ten quality samples and a 100-order conversion test first. Expand marketing after sales evidence, retaining funding for fulfillment and refunds.</p>\n<h3>Monthly funding illustration</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Month</th><th scope=\"col\">Fulfilled revenue</th><th scope=\"col\">Economic spending</th><th scope=\"col\">Cumulative balance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>29,900</td><td>45,792</td><td>-15,892</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>89,700</td><td>58,776</td><td>15,032</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>179,400</td><td>86,352</td><td>108,080</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Assumes all due sales settle in the same month and planned costs are paid. These month-end balances do not establish daily peak funding; deposits, holds, deferred delivery and taxes require an actual dated cash ledger. Working capital is financing, not an additional P&amp;L cost.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":13,"title":"90-day milestones","lead":"Plan 100 / 300 / 600 accepted orders; unfulfilled prepayments do not meet the profit goal.","body":"D7: two authorized stories, playable cases, scope and logs. D14: ten samples, 20 genuine quotations, validate the first ten paid orders. D30: accept 100 orders with ten attributable channels. D60: accept 300 more, expand to 30 channels and prepare three delivery contributors. D90: accept 600 more, totaling 1,000; reconcile price mix and the 108,080 target surplus.\n\nIf authors play without buying, reassess demand and price. If polished mix falls below 20%, use the actual order value rather than inventing premium orders. Later 10,000/100,000 paid-author stages require proven automation, CAC and capacity.","sources":[],"requirements":["R3","R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>D7: two authorized stories, playable cases, scope and logs. D14: ten samples, 20 genuine quotations, validate the first ten paid orders. D30: accept 100 orders with ten attributable channels. D60: accept 300 more, expand to 30 channels and prepare three delivery contributors. D90: accept 600 more, totaling 1,000; reconcile price mix and the 108,080 target surplus.</p>\n<p>If authors play without buying, reassess demand and price. If polished mix falls below 20%, use the actual order value rather than inventing premium orders. Later 10,000/100,000 paid-author stages require proven automation, CAC and capacity.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":14,"title":"Metrics & acceptance criteria","lead":"Assess payment, fulfillment, cost and quality together rather than revenue alone.","body":"1,000 accepted paid works; target 80/20 price mix; preview-to-paid 10%; full CAC ≤40; generation completion ≥95%; zero serious privacy incidents.\n\nThese are proposed thresholds. Count unique valid payers, remove invalid/refunded transactions, and accept only usable confirmed outputs. Separate mature observation periods. Track source, reach, unique visits, actual payment, delivery, refunds and full cost. Downloads and intent are not revenue. Pause expansion and revise the plan if early pricing, quality or unit-cost gates fail.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>1,000 accepted paid works; target 80/20 price mix; preview-to-paid 10%; full CAC ≤40; generation completion ≥95%; zero serious privacy incidents.</p>\n<p>These are proposed thresholds. Count unique valid payers, remove invalid/refunded transactions, and accept only usable confirmed outputs. Separate mature observation periods. Track source, reach, unique visits, actual payment, delivery, refunds and full cost. Downloads and intent are not revenue. Pause expansion and revise the plan if early pricing, quality or unit-cost gates fail.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":15,"title":"Risks & responses","lead":"Story quality, generation cost and rights to personal material determine whether the service can continue.","body":"| Risk | Early signal | Response / responsibility |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Incomplete work | Dead branches, missing endings or assets | Engineering validates reachability; no unfinished delivery |\n| Inconsistent characters | Names, relationships or images change | I design confirmation steps; author accepts the work |\n| Cost escalation | Image retries, long expansion, unlimited editing | Cap scope and revisions; quote additions |\n| Privacy / rights | Unapproved photos, chats or third-party material | Private by default; de-identify and confirm permission; sharing can be withdrawn |\n| Sharing fails to convert | Views without new authors | Diagnose creation friction; views are not growth |\n| Infrequent demand | Occasion-only purchases and little repeat use | Consider per-work gift service rather than monthly subscription |\n\n### Fact and fiction\nAI-added dialogue and alternative-choice scenes must be identified as creative material, not real chats, real reactions or predictions of a life. Preserve generation labels in the experience and export.\n\n### Stop conditions\nPause open recruitment if generation cost consistently exceeds what price supports, source rights cannot be explained, or a serious privacy issue occurs. Address causes and affected works first.","sources":["S12"],"requirements":["R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Risk</th><th scope=\"col\">Early signal</th><th scope=\"col\">Response / responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Incomplete work</td><td>Dead branches, missing endings or assets</td><td>Engineering validates reachability; no unfinished delivery</td></tr><tr><td>Inconsistent characters</td><td>Names, relationships or images change</td><td>I design confirmation steps; author accepts the work</td></tr><tr><td>Cost escalation</td><td>Image retries, long expansion, unlimited editing</td><td>Cap scope and revisions; quote additions</td></tr><tr><td>Privacy / rights</td><td>Unapproved photos, chats or third-party material</td><td>Private by default; de-identify and confirm permission; sharing can be withdrawn</td></tr><tr><td>Sharing fails to convert</td><td>Views without new authors</td><td>Diagnose creation friction; views are not growth</td></tr><tr><td>Infrequent demand</td><td>Occasion-only purchases and little repeat use</td><td>Consider per-work gift service rather than monthly subscription</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Fact and fiction</h3>\n<p>AI-added dialogue and alternative-choice scenes must be identified as creative material, not real chats, real reactions or predictions of a life. Preserve generation labels in the experience and export.</p>\n<h3>Stop conditions</h3>\n<p>Pause open recruitment if generation cost consistently exceeds what price supports, source rights cannot be explained, or a serious privacy issue occurs. Address causes and affected works first.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":16,"title":"Team roles & collaboration","lead":"I will lead product and market execution, while assessing technical choices and resources jointly with the team.","body":"### My proposed responsibilities\nI will own character and narrative experience, work specifications, author recruitment and sample delivery. I can rapidly prototype and prepare experiments with AI, and want to assess reliability, costs and scalable implementation with engineering. A prototype is not proof of production-service readiness.\n\n| Role | Proposed responsibility | To confirm |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 最高 | Product, customers/users, market work, experiments and review | Availability and stage targets |\n| Engineering lead | Architecture, models/tools, permissions, tasks and cost logs | People, hours, schedule and maintenance |\n| Professional / content reviewer | Facts, asset rights and output quality | Reviewer, competence, price and scope |\n| Customer / user | Usable material, confirmation, feedback and acceptance | Consent and intended use |\n| Team247 lead | Budget, resources, payment/contract entity and stage decisions | Authority and available resources |\n\n### Decisions to make together\nLaunch platform, core tasks, models/tools, usage budget, data handling, release requirements, price, responsibilities and acceptance. Joint discussion is not an excuse to provide no proposal: this BP offers comparable assumptions and experiments for the team to revise.\n\n### Working cadence\nReview real activations/customers, payments/refunds, output quality, effort/API costs and next-week decisions weekly. Record a continue/adjust/pause decision at days 14 and 30. These are proposals, not staffing or budget commitments already obtained.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<h3>My proposed responsibilities</h3>\n<p>I will own character and narrative experience, work specifications, author recruitment and sample delivery. I can rapidly prototype and prepare experiments with AI, and want to assess reliability, costs and scalable implementation with engineering. A prototype is not proof of production-service readiness.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Role</th><th scope=\"col\">Proposed responsibility</th><th scope=\"col\">To confirm</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>最高</td><td>Product, customers/users, market work, experiments and review</td><td>Availability and stage targets</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering lead</td><td>Architecture, models/tools, permissions, tasks and cost logs</td><td>People, hours, schedule and maintenance</td></tr><tr><td>Professional / content reviewer</td><td>Facts, asset rights and output quality</td><td>Reviewer, competence, price and scope</td></tr><tr><td>Customer / user</td><td>Usable material, confirmation, feedback and acceptance</td><td>Consent and intended use</td></tr><tr><td>Team247 lead</td><td>Budget, resources, payment/contract entity and stage decisions</td><td>Authority and available resources</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Decisions to make together</h3>\n<p>Launch platform, core tasks, models/tools, usage budget, data handling, release requirements, price, responsibilities and acceptance. Joint discussion is not an excuse to provide no proposal: this BP offers comparable assumptions and experiments for the team to revise.</p>\n<h3>Working cadence</h3>\n<p>Review real activations/customers, payments/refunds, output quality, effort/API costs and next-week decisions weekly. Record a continue/adjust/pause decision at days 14 and 30. These are proposals, not staffing or budget commitments already obtained.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":17,"title":"Evidence, assumptions & unknowns","lead":"Public sources support context and constraints. Project revenue and growth remain unverified assumptions.","body":"| Evidence | Date and limits |\n| --- | --- |\n| [S1 · CNNIC: 2026 generative AI application report](https://www2.cnnic.cn/n4/2026/1008/c326-11703.html) | Published 2026-10-08; first half of 2026. Official indexed summary only; direct body retrieval timed out. More than 700 million AI users is context, not the size of this paying segment. |\n| [S8 · AI Dungeon official memberships](https://help.aidungeon.com/memberships-benefits) | Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09. Journey USD 14.99/month and tiered plans. This does not validate local pricing for personal visual novels. |\n| [S9 · Ren'Py official website](https://www.renpy.org/) | Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09. Open-source visual-novel engine, free for commercial use. Other assets and production do not become free. |\n| [S12 · Measures for labeling AI-generated synthetic content](https://www.cac.gov.cn/2025-03/14/c_1743654684782215.htm) | Published March 2025; effective 2025-09-01. Explicit and implicit labeling requirements. This does not mean any required filing or approval has been completed. |\n\n### Critical gaps\nReal author demand; generation retries and review time; paid/repeat purchase; sharing-to-creation conversion; rights to character material; cost of the first free work.\n\n### Replace assumptions with evidence\nUse sourced prospect records, interviews, payment/refund records, task logs, supplier invoices and mature-cohort observations. Mark missing evidence as unverified; do not invent customers, case-study revenue, permissions or testimonials.\n\n### Evidence levels\nPublic facts retain their sources and dates. Prices, counts and costs are planning assumptions. Formula outputs are calculations. Relationships, resources and technical capability remain to be validated. Recheck dynamic prices before launch. The BP and website are deliverables; commercial viability has not been established.\n\nNew target gaps: accepted quotations, attributable reach, actual payment/refunds, full labor/API costs, delivery capacity and team resources. Page 11 economics V7 supersedes earlier figures; public sources do not establish project sales.","sources":["S1","S8","S9","S12"],"requirements":["R1","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Evidence</th><th scope=\"col\">Date and limits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://www2.cnnic.cn/n4/2026/1008/c326-11703.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S1 · CNNIC: 2026 generative AI application report</a></td><td>Published 2026-10-08; first half of 2026. Official indexed summary only; direct body retrieval timed out. More than 700 million AI users is context, not the size of this paying segment.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://help.aidungeon.com/memberships-benefits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S8 · AI Dungeon official memberships</a></td><td>Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09. Journey USD 14.99/month and tiered plans. This does not validate local pricing for personal visual novels.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.renpy.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S9 · Ren&#x27;Py official website</a></td><td>Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09. Open-source visual-novel engine, free for commercial use. Other assets and production do not become free.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.cac.gov.cn/2025-03/14/c_1743654684782215.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">S12 · Measures for labeling AI-generated synthetic content</a></td><td>Published March 2025; effective 2025-09-01. Explicit and implicit labeling requirements. This does not mean any required filing or approval has been completed.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Critical gaps</h3>\n<p>Real author demand; generation retries and review time; paid/repeat purchase; sharing-to-creation conversion; rights to character material; cost of the first free work.</p>\n<h3>Replace assumptions with evidence</h3>\n<p>Use sourced prospect records, interviews, payment/refund records, task logs, supplier invoices and mature-cohort observations. Mark missing evidence as unverified; do not invent customers, case-study revenue, permissions or testimonials.</p>\n<h3>Evidence levels</h3>\n<p>Public facts retain their sources and dates. Prices, counts and costs are planning assumptions. Formula outputs are calculations. Relationships, resources and technical capability remain to be validated. Recheck dynamic prices before launch. The BP and website are deliverables; commercial viability has not been established.</p>\n<p>New target gaps: accepted quotations, attributable reach, actual payment/refunds, full labor/API costs, delivery capacity and team resources. Page 11 economics V7 supersedes earlier figures; public sources do not establish project sales.</p>","appendixHtml":""},{"number":18,"title":"Recommendation & decisions","lead":"Organize resources around the larger commercial objective; target economic surplus of CNY 108,080.00 requires its assumptions to hold.","body":"Use 199 standard plus 699 polished to support order value. Complete ten samples and validate 100 paid authors before expanding to 1,000.\n\nConfirm owners, available labor, technical route, budget, operating/tax entity, channels and stop gates together. I will drive product, market, content and validation. These are the business outcomes to pursue; orders, reach and costs still require evidence. Recalculate actual results when targets are missed rather than promising profit.","sources":[],"requirements":["R4","R5"],"appendix":[],"appendixText":"","html":"<p>Use 199 standard plus 699 polished to support order value. Complete ten samples and validate 100 paid authors before expanding to 1,000.</p>\n<p>Confirm owners, available labor, technical route, budget, operating/tax entity, channels and stop gates together. I will drive product, market, content and validation. These are the business outcomes to pursue; orders, reach and costs still require evidence. Recalculate actual results when targets are missed rather than promising profit.</p>","appendixHtml":""}]}],"sources":[{"id":"S1","title":"CNNIC: 2026 generative AI application report","url":"https://www2.cnnic.cn/n4/2026/1008/c326-11703.html","date":"Published 2026-10-08; first half of 2026","note":"Official indexed summary only; direct body retrieval timed out. More than 700 million AI users is context, not the size of this paying segment."},{"id":"S2","title":"National Health Commission: 2024 statistical bulletin","url":"https://www.nhc.gov.cn/guihuaxxs/c100132/202512/9db8db5488a748c4b1e1068a4a8c4455.shtml?menuid=128","date":"Published December 2025; year-end 2024 statistics","note":"38,710 total hospitals and 26,956 private hospitals. These are not medical-aesthetics institution counts."},{"id":"S3","title":"Character.AI subscription page","url":"https://character.ai/subscribe","date":"Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09","note":"USD 94.99 annual price and feature tiers. This does not establish willingness to pay in China."},{"id":"S4","title":"Character.AI official promotion terms","url":"https://support.character.ai/hc/en-us/articles/51248493096987-c-ai-Summer-Flash-Sale-Offer-Terms","date":"Updated 2026-06-05","note":"Terms state a regular USD 9.99/month renewal price. This does not mean the promotion remains available or all regions share one price."},{"id":"S5","title":"Replika official product page","url":"https://replika.com/","date":"Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09","note":"AI-companion positioning. Promotional user counts were not treated as paying-user scale."},{"id":"S6","title":"Dify official pricing","url":"https://dify.ai/pricing","date":"Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09","note":"Annual Professional USD 590/workspace and Team USD 1,590. These are not the total cost of an industry service."},{"id":"S7","title":"Coze official plans and pricing","url":"https://docs.coze.cn/cozespace_coze_billing_overview","date":"Checked 2026-11-09; page announces changes on November 12","note":"Subscriptions and credits. Near-term price changes mean these are not a fixed long-term API cost."},{"id":"S8","title":"AI Dungeon official memberships","url":"https://help.aidungeon.com/memberships-benefits","date":"Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09","note":"Journey USD 14.99/month and tiered plans. This does not validate local pricing for personal visual novels."},{"id":"S9","title":"Ren'Py official website","url":"https://www.renpy.org/","date":"Dynamic page; checked 2026-11-09","note":"Open-source visual-novel engine, free for commercial use. Other assets and production do not become free."},{"id":"S10","title":"Medical-aesthetics advertising enforcement guidance","url":"https://www.samr.gov.cn/zw/zfxxgk/fdzdgknr/ggjgs/art/2023/art_d1b46dbc27214abcace53a0ec539f7bb.html","date":"2021 guidance; migrated official page","note":"Qualifications, review and content restrictions. Human checking is not regulatory approval."},{"id":"S11","title":"Medical advertising supervision guidance","url":"https://www.samr.gov.cn/zw/zfxxgk/fdzdgknr/ggjgs/art/2025/art_cd56662cf13b4ad59eabfe31cb1122e1.html","date":"Published May 2025","note":"Informs advertising-review boundaries; it is not a compliance determination for this product."},{"id":"S12","title":"Measures for labeling AI-generated synthetic content","url":"https://www.cac.gov.cn/2025-03/14/c_1743654684782215.htm","date":"Published March 2025; effective 2025-09-01","note":"Explicit and implicit labeling requirements. This does not mean any required filing or approval has been completed."},{"id":"S13","title":"Apple App Review Guidelines","url":"https://developer.apple.com/app-store/review/guidelines/","date":"Checked 2026-11-09","note":"Paid functionality, incentives and store rules need assessment for the relevant region and actual mechanism; cash rewards cannot be assumed launchable unchanged."},{"id":"S14","title":"Ministry of Justice: Regulations on Prohibition of Pyramid Selling","url":"https://xzfg.moj.gov.cn/front/law/detail?LawID=148","date":"Searched 2026-11-09","note":"Recruiting eligibility purchased through payment and compensation linked to recruitment or levels require assessment. A single referral level does not automatically establish compliance."},{"id":"S15","title":"Doubao official feature introduction","url":"https://www.doubao.com/legal/feature_intro","date":"Official indexed summary checked 2026-11-09","note":"Assistant, voice and text capabilities. No pricing or user data from imitation websites is used."},{"id":"S16","title":"Apple Intelligence developer introduction","url":"https://developer.apple.com/cn/apple-intelligence/","date":"Official indexed summary checked 2026-11-09","note":"Personal context, app actions and system entry points are competitive references. Region/device availability requires separate verification."},{"id":"S17","title":"Tencent TokenHub pricing","url":"https://cloud.tencent.com/document/product/1823/130055/","date":"2026-11-09","note":"Input/output token billing varies by model and region. Supports cost methodology, not product quality or the target cost."}],"common":{"comparison":{"title":"Comparison & priorities","lead":"Larger commercial objectives, with explicit conditions and downside cases.","body":"### Target-led comparison\nAll amounts in CNY. These are operating targets requiring real distribution, price acceptance and measured costs.\n\n### Personal AI for everyday life\n| Scenario / stage | Paying customers | Revenue | Total budget | Target economic surplus |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Conservative | 30,000 | 30,000.00 | 33,200.00 | -3,200.00 |\n| Target | 100,000 | 100,000.00 | 50,000.00 | 50,000.00 |\n| Stretch | 200,000 | 200,000.00 | 74,000.00 | 126,000.00 |\n| One-million stage | 1,000,000 | 1,000,000.00 | 360,000.00 | 640,000.00 |\n| Ten-million stage | 10,000,000 | 10,000,000.00 | 3,400,000.00 | 6,600,000.00 |\n\n### AI agent for medical aesthetics\n| Scenario / stage | Paying customers | Revenue | Total budget | Target economic surplus |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Conservative | 4 | 92,800.00 | 108,224.00 | -15,424.00 |\n| Target | 12 | 292,000.00 | 189,360.00 | 102,640.00 |\n| Stretch | 20 | 504,800.00 | 289,184.00 | 215,616.00 |\n\n### Personal-story visual novels\n| Scenario / stage | Paying customers | Revenue | Total budget | Target economic surplus |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Conservative | 200 | 59,800.00 | 86,784.00 | -26,984.00 |\n| Target | 1,000 | 299,000.00 | 190,920.00 | 108,080.00 |\n| Stretch | 3,000 | 897,000.00 | 477,760.00 | 419,240.00 |\n### Basis of calculation\nThis is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit.\n\nConsumer scale: personal AI; near-term high-value paid delivery: industry; creative consumer revenue: stories. Select a lead direction and named resources rather than assuming all budgets are funded together.","html":"<h3>Target-led comparison</h3>\n<p>All amounts in CNY. These are operating targets requiring real distribution, price acceptance and measured costs.</p>\n<h3>Personal AI for everyday life</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Scenario / stage</th><th scope=\"col\">Paying customers</th><th scope=\"col\">Revenue</th><th scope=\"col\">Total budget</th><th scope=\"col\">Target economic surplus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Conservative</td><td>30,000</td><td>30,000.00</td><td>33,200.00</td><td>-3,200.00</td></tr><tr><td>Target</td><td>100,000</td><td>100,000.00</td><td>50,000.00</td><td>50,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Stretch</td><td>200,000</td><td>200,000.00</td><td>74,000.00</td><td>126,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>One-million stage</td><td>1,000,000</td><td>1,000,000.00</td><td>360,000.00</td><td>640,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Ten-million stage</td><td>10,000,000</td><td>10,000,000.00</td><td>3,400,000.00</td><td>6,600,000.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>AI agent for medical aesthetics</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Scenario / stage</th><th scope=\"col\">Paying customers</th><th scope=\"col\">Revenue</th><th scope=\"col\">Total budget</th><th scope=\"col\">Target economic surplus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Conservative</td><td>4</td><td>92,800.00</td><td>108,224.00</td><td>-15,424.00</td></tr><tr><td>Target</td><td>12</td><td>292,000.00</td><td>189,360.00</td><td>102,640.00</td></tr><tr><td>Stretch</td><td>20</td><td>504,800.00</td><td>289,184.00</td><td>215,616.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Personal-story visual novels</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数据表，可在表内横向滚动\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Scenario / stage</th><th scope=\"col\">Paying customers</th><th scope=\"col\">Revenue</th><th scope=\"col\">Total budget</th><th scope=\"col\">Target economic surplus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Conservative</td><td>200</td><td>59,800.00</td><td>86,784.00</td><td>-26,984.00</td></tr><tr><td>Target</td><td>1,000</td><td>299,000.00</td><td>190,920.00</td><td>108,080.00</td></tr><tr><td>Stretch</td><td>3,000</td><td>897,000.00</td><td>477,760.00</td><td>419,240.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Basis of calculation</h3>\n<p>This is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit.</p>\n<p>Consumer scale: personal AI; near-term high-value paid delivery: industry; creative consumer revenue: stories. Select a lead direction and named resources rather than assuming all budgets are funded together.</p>"},"feedback":{"title":"Responses to the review requests","lead":"A substantive response to the feedback supplied by 最高, with direct links to the relevant pages. Private chat screenshots are not reproduced.","body":"### R1 — Market and investment\nPersonal AI: 100,000/200,000 payers in 90 days; later one million/ten million. Industry: 400 qualified prospects toward 12 implementations. Stories: 50,000 visits toward 1,000 paid authors. Pages 05, 09 and 12 give sources, funnels and full budgets.\n### R2 — Price and fulfillment\nCNY 1 capped personal-AI entry; 19,800 industry implementation plus 6,800/month; 199/699 story tiers. Pages 04, 07 and 08 specify entitlements, costs and value.\n### R3 — Acquisition and marketing\nEarly 100/1,000-user checks validate channels rather than limit ambition. Page 09 contains the updated reach, conversion and CAC; page 10 covers referrals/sales and page 13 the 90-day schedule.\n### R4 — Priority and profitability\nTarget 50,000 personal-AI, 102,640 industry and 108,080 story economic surplus. These are conditional goals, not guaranteed net profits. Comparison and pages 11–14/18 show what must be true and when to pause.\n### R5 — Reproducible review\nPrompt V3 precedes the revised models. Eleven scenario rows, full cost breakdowns, downloadable inputs and a reproduction script support review. Full CNY 1 rewards are shown as a loss-making alternative, not silently mixed into the capped target.\n","html":"<h3>R1 — Market and investment</h3>\n<p>Personal AI: 100,000/200,000 payers in 90 days; later one million/ten million. Industry: 400 qualified prospects toward 12 implementations. Stories: 50,000 visits toward 1,000 paid authors. Pages 05, 09 and 12 give sources, funnels and full budgets.</p>\n<h3>R2 — Price and fulfillment</h3>\n<p>CNY 1 capped personal-AI entry; 19,800 industry implementation plus 6,800/month; 199/699 story tiers. Pages 04, 07 and 08 specify entitlements, costs and value.</p>\n<h3>R3 — Acquisition and marketing</h3>\n<p>Early 100/1,000-user checks validate channels rather than limit ambition. Page 09 contains the updated reach, conversion and CAC; page 10 covers referrals/sales and page 13 the 90-day schedule.</p>\n<h3>R4 — Priority and profitability</h3>\n<p>Target 50,000 personal-AI, 102,640 industry and 108,080 story economic surplus. These are conditional goals, not guaranteed net profits. Comparison and pages 11–14/18 show what must be true and when to pause.</p>\n<h3>R5 — Reproducible review</h3>\n<p>Prompt V3 precedes the revised models. Eleven scenario rows, full cost breakdowns, downloadable inputs and a reproduction script support review. Full CNY 1 rewards are shown as a loss-making alternative, not silently mixed into the capped target.</p>"},"method":{"title":"Definitions, data & attachments","lead":"These are plans and models for joint decisions, not evidence of actual customers, payments, permissions or committed staffing.","body":"### Basis of calculation\nThis is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit.\n\n### Current version\nV7 and economics Prompt V3 replace all earlier economics, including the CNY 29 personal assistant and 2,980/1,980 industry pilot. Download the complete new model and script below. Historical files retain their original language and assumptions. No actual sales or campaigns have been executed.","html":"<h3>Basis of calculation</h3>\n<p>This is a target-led operating plan. Prices, sales, conversion and cost ceilings remain untested. Economic surplus equals fulfilled revenue less the full economic budget, including paid labor, build, marketing, service, processing and tax/refund reserves. Reserves are not final tax settlements. Actual net profit depends on the operating entity, contracts and accounting. Unfulfilled prepayments are deferred rather than counted as profit.</p>\n<h3>Current version</h3>\n<p>V7 and economics Prompt V3 replace all earlier economics, including the CNY 29 personal assistant and 2,980/1,980 industry pilot. Download the complete new model and script below. Historical files retain their original language and assumptions. No actual sales or campaigns have been executed.</p>"}},"requirements":{"R1":"Market & investment evidence","R2":"Pricing & delivery cost","R3":"First customers & growth","R4":"Priority & validation","R5":"Comparable review materials"},"economics":[{"project":"persona","scenario":"保守","paid_customers":30000,"revenue":30000,"costs":{"build_and_operations":26000,"service_allowance":3000.0,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":1200.0,"seed_and_content_marketing":1500.0,"capped_referral_pool":1500.0},"total_cost":33200.0,"target_surplus":-3200.0,"unit_contribution":0.76,"break_even":34211,"period":"90-day launch target"},{"project":"persona","scenario":"目标","paid_customers":100000,"revenue":100000,"costs":{"build_and_operations":26000,"service_allowance":10000.0,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":4000.0,"seed_and_content_marketing":5000.0,"capped_referral_pool":5000.0},"total_cost":50000.0,"target_surplus":50000.0,"unit_contribution":0.76,"break_even":34211,"period":"90-day launch target"},{"project":"persona","scenario":"冲刺","paid_customers":200000,"revenue":200000,"costs":{"build_and_operations":26000,"service_allowance":20000.0,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":8000.0,"seed_and_content_marketing":10000.0,"capped_referral_pool":10000.0},"total_cost":74000.0,"target_surplus":126000.0,"unit_contribution":0.76,"break_even":34211,"period":"90-day launch target"},{"project":"persona","scenario":"百万阶段","paid_customers":1000000,"revenue":1000000,"costs":{"build_and_operations":120000,"service_allowance":100000.0,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":40000.0,"seed_and_content_marketing":50000.0,"capped_referral_pool":50000.0},"total_cost":360000.0,"target_surplus":640000.0,"unit_contribution":0.76,"break_even":157895,"period":"later-stage standalone capacity illustration"},{"project":"persona","scenario":"千万阶段","paid_customers":10000000,"revenue":10000000,"costs":{"build_and_operations":1000000,"service_allowance":1000000.0,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":400000.0,"seed_and_content_marketing":500000.0,"capped_referral_pool":500000.0},"total_cost":3400000.0,"target_surplus":6600000.0,"unit_contribution":0.76,"break_even":1315790,"period":"later-stage standalone capacity illustration"},{"project":"industry","scenario":"保守","paid_customers":4,"revenue":92800,"costs":{"implementation_delivery":19200,"subscription_delivery":3600,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":7424.0,"sales_marketing":20000,"build":40000,"operations":18000},"total_cost":108224.0,"target_surplus":-15424.0,"subscription_customer_months":2,"period":"90 days after resource approval"},{"project":"industry","scenario":"目标","paid_customers":12,"revenue":292000,"costs":{"implementation_delivery":57600,"subscription_delivery":14400,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":23360.0,"sales_marketing":36000,"build":40000,"operations":18000},"total_cost":189360.0,"target_surplus":102640.0,"subscription_customer_months":8,"period":"90 days after resource approval"},{"project":"industry","scenario":"冲刺","paid_customers":20,"revenue":504800,"costs":{"implementation_delivery":96000,"subscription_delivery":28800,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":40384.0,"sales_marketing":60000,"build":40000,"operations":24000},"total_cost":289184.0,"target_surplus":215616.0,"subscription_customer_months":16,"period":"90 days after resource approval"},{"project":"story","scenario":"保守","paid_customers":200,"revenue":59800,"costs":{"paid_work_delivery":16000,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":4784.0,"marketing":20000,"free_samples":1000,"build":30000,"operations":15000},"total_cost":86784.0,"target_surplus":-26984.0,"standard_orders":160,"premium_orders":40,"period":"90-day selling and delivery window"},{"project":"story","scenario":"目标","paid_customers":1000,"revenue":299000,"costs":{"paid_work_delivery":80000,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":23920.0,"marketing":40000,"free_samples":2000,"build":30000,"operations":15000},"total_cost":190920.0,"target_surplus":108080.0,"standard_orders":800,"premium_orders":200,"period":"90-day selling and delivery window"},{"project":"story","scenario":"冲刺","paid_customers":3000,"revenue":897000,"costs":{"paid_work_delivery":240000,"payment_tax_refund_reserve":71760.0,"marketing":100000,"free_samples":6000,"build":30000,"operations":30000},"total_cost":477760.0,"target_surplus":419240.0,"standard_orders":2400,"premium_orders":600,"period":"90-day selling and delivery window"}],"financeLabels":{"title":"Inspect scenario costs","note":"All cases are target-led assumptions; later scale stages are not 90-day forecasts.","scenario":"Scenario","item":"Item","amount":"CNY","revenue":"Revenue","cost":"Total economic budget","surplus":"Target economic surplus","scenes":{"保守":"Conservative","目标":"Target","冲刺":"Stretch","百万阶段":"One-million stage","千万阶段":"Ten-million stage"},"costs":{"build_and_operations":"Build and operating labor","service_allowance":"Service allowance","payment_tax_refund_reserve":"Processing / tax / refund reserve","seed_and_content_marketing":"Seed/content marketing","capped_referral_pool":"Capped referral pool","implementation_delivery":"Implementation delivery","subscription_delivery":"Subscription delivery","sales_marketing":"Sales/marketing","build":"Build","operations":"Operations","paid_work_delivery":"Paid-work delivery","marketing":"Marketing","free_samples":"Free samples"}},"coverNote":"Personal AI targets 100,000 paying users in 90 days, stretches to 200,000, then plans for one million and ten million. All three proposals use larger commercial targets with explicit pricing, marketing, full costs and conditions.","promptHtml":"<h2>最高 × Team247 | Economics Prompt V3</h2>\n<p>Write this prompt before revising the business plans. Preserve the formal paginated website, full English/Chinese editions and English default.</p>\n<p>Act as the business analyst, growth planner and financial modeler. Rebuild all three economic models around the updated ambition. Work backward from targets into testable conditions; do not present desired profits as verified forecasts.</p>\n<ol><li>Personal AI: target at least 100,000 real paying users in 90 days, stretch 200,000. At CNY 1 first payment, revenue is 100,000/200,000. Target a full 50,000 economic budget and 50,000 surplus at the 100,000 stage, including build, labor, models, payment, marketing, rewards and tax/refund reserves. Plan later one-million and ten-million payer stages without invented dates. Define registration, activation, payment and exactly what the entry price buys.</li><li>Reconcile the referral conflict. Returning CNY 1 on every CNY 1 purchase leaves nothing for other costs. Show that original mechanism&#x27;s loss as a comparison and propose an explicitly capped first reward experiment. Do not imply the user already agreed to this change: the target requires team acceptance. Do not fill gaps with unsupported subscriptions or sponsorship.</li><li>Industry agent: offer a higher-value, bounded implementation and monthly service. Show prices, delivery, measurable customer ROI, 90-day revenue recognition and receipt timing. Target six-figure CNY economic surplus; allow conservative losses. The prospect funnel, cycle, reviewer hours and capacity must support the sales plan.</li><li>Visual novels: combine a larger paid-author base with tiered order value. Define standard/polished specifications, mix, marketing funnel, free sample costs, retries, rights, review and delivery capacity. Target six-figure CNY surplus. Player views are not paying authors.</li><li>Each proposal needs conservative/target/stretch cases, monthly milestones, full costs, break-even, price/sales/CAC/unit-cost sensitivities, funding and start conditions. Defer unfulfilled revenue; prepayments are not profit. Tax/refund reserves are assumptions, not final net-profit accounting.</li><li>Label values as targets, budget ceilings, quotation hypotheses or calculated results. Supplier quotations, traffic, conversion, payment, renewal and costs require actual evidence. Macro adoption and competitors do not prove sales.</li><li>Update linked summary, market, scope, price, cost, acquisition, finance, resources, milestones, metrics and decisions, plus comparison, review responses, downloads and prompt. Earlier low-price/loss models are historical only. Both languages use identical figures and reproducible scripts.</li><li>Verify all pages, financial identities, language switching, finance interaction, mobile layout and deployment. Do not claim AGI has validated demand or guarantees profitability.</li></ol>"};
